TestLink - 2.0.1 (2026 Q3) (Released 2026-09)
===================================================

TestLink Upgraded 2.0.1 is a modernization release of the TestLink 1.9.20
codebase: the legacy Smarty UI was rewritten into a modern Dashio Bootstrap
single-page HTML/JS/CSS front-end backed by a plain-PHP REST BFF API layer.
Every screen of the application was ported one-by-one in a screen-compare
(legacy 1.9.20 <-> modern) feature-parity process. The legacy code base was
kept for backward compatibility and is progressively retired as each modern
screen reaches full parity.

- [KEY BUGFIX] - #1876: **the mandated suite gate `ai/verify_test_suites.sh` check 2b counted a
  restored EOF newline as "1 line removed", so EVERY append to `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md` failed
  while the baseline is unterminated.** The clobber lineage (#1849/#1851) left the shared suite
  file without a trailing newline at `origin/sebiboga`; GNU `diff` reports `last-line` vs
  `last-line\n` as a change (`2c` + `\ No newline at end of file`), so the check's
  `diff base cand | grep -c '^<'` returned 1 for any legitimate append (measured on the Issue
  #1686 suite restore: `FAIL no line removed … (= 1) - < existing-but-denied writes.`,
  `GATE_EXIT=1`). Fix (1 file, +10/-2): normalise the final newline on both sides
  (`awk '{print}' "$1"`) before the diff — in the check and in its diagnostic re-run.
  Detection preserved, verified with negative tests: 1 removed baseline line → FAIL (=1) with
  the line printed, 5 removed → FAIL (=5), append-only → PASS (=0); an intermediate draft that
  dropped the awk argument emptied both sides and passed unconditionally, caught by the same
  tests before commit. Checks 2a (heading set-difference, #1805) and 2c untouched. Found while
  merging stale branch `fix/issue-1686`, which restored the Issue #1686 regression suite
  (9 cases, `TC-1686-01..09`) clobbered from the default branch — the branch's docs page and
  screenshot were already on `sebiboga` (`cea77d944`, byte-identical). Gate after fix:
  7 PASS / 0 FAIL, baseline 44 → 45 suites. (Fixes #1876, Refs #1686)

- [KEY BUGFIX] - #1875: **7 `ftc.*` keys of the modernized Free Test Cases screen
  (`freeTestCases.html`) rendered untranslated English in 8 of the 10 locale bundles.**
  `ftc.allAssigned`, `ftc.elapsedSeconds`, `ftc.forProject`, `ftc.header`, `ftc.matchCount`,
  `ftc.testCases`, `ftc.testProject` were copied byte-identical to `en.json` during the
  #1262/#1265 batches; the #1844 coverage gate compares key SETS only, so a present-but-English
  value passes silently. Fix (`29cc40397` on `fix/issue-1875-ftc-i18n`): translate the 7 keys in
  de/es/fr/it/ja/pt/ru/zh, each value reusing that locale's existing terminology already present
  in the same bundles (`ato.testProject`, `ato.forProject`, `dsh.testCases`/`cwt.testCases`,
  `reqsearch.matchCount`, `reqcov.elapsedSeconds`) and the legacy `locale/*/strings.txt`;
  `ftc.groupHeader` intentionally left identical (placeholder template). Verified: json.tool +
  coverage gate 9/9 green, cross-bundle diff 0 identical keys, browser de+zh render fully
  localized, Event Viewer clean; regression suite 8/8 PASS. (Refs #1875)

- [KEY BUGFIX] - #1804: **the per-row reorder controls of `reqTreeReorder.html` (Up / Down / To top /
  To bottom) were non-interactive `<span class="rm dis">` elements, not real `<button disabled>`** —
  a `<span>` is not focusable and never enters the tab order, `.prop('disabled', …)` in
  `applyRowState()` is a silent no-op on it, there is no `aria-disabled` for assistive technology,
  no tooltip saying WHY a control is dead, and (before the fix) no `pointer-events: none`, so a click
  on a disabled control still dispatched and only `nudge()`'s bounds check stopped it. Fix
  (`4f074a2b5`, also `dfd74229d` on `fix/issue-1804`): `btn()` now builds `button[type="button"]`
  with `disabled` + `aria-disabled="true"` + an edge-row `title`, and
  `.rm.dis, .rm:disabled { …; pointer-events: none }` keeps a dead control out of the pointer chain;
  the `reqtr.alreadyFirst` / `reqtr.alreadyLast` tooltip keys were later added to all 10 locale
  bundles and resolved through `TLi18n.has()` by #1829. The issue's regression suite had been lost
  from `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md` by the `136fc4426` full-file clobber and is restored by the merge of
  `fix/issue-1804`. (Fixes #1804)

- [KEY BUGFIX] - #1712: **eight sibling issue-tracker interfaces (mantissoap, jirasoap, jirarest,
  fogbugzrest, gforgesoap, redminerest, tracxmlrpc, tuleaprest) answered HTTP 502 on
  `POST /api/issuetracker/test-connection`** whenever a structurally-string cfg member came back
  from `setCfg()`'s SimpleXML→json→stdClass round-trip as a nested object (element-valued,
  empty, whitespace-only or repeated XML field): the unguarded `(string)`/`trim()` read threw an
  `\Error`/`\TypeError` that `catch(Exception)` cannot catch, and the Event Viewer only showed
  `Object of class stdClass could not be converted to string` with no field name. #1711's guard
  existed but was **private to `bugzillaxmlrpcInterface`** — it now lives on the base class
  (`protected cfgStr()/cfgIsNotText()/cfgWarn()` + new `cfgCoerceText()`), the shadowing private
  copies were deleted, and all eight classes normalise every cfg member before reading. Code
  review additionally closed 5 remaining `trim($this->cfg->uribase,"/")` sites (same 502) and
  4 raw credential reads. A non-text field is now named in a WARNING row and the request returns
  HTTP 200; a valid scalar cfg is byte-identical to before. Verified: `tmp/repro_1712.php`
  14/14 PASS (pre-fix 11 failures), `tmp/verify_1712.sh` 25/25 PASS, all 8 types HTTP 200,
  0 fatal-signature Event rows, grid/list/`check-connection` unaffected. Docs:
  `docs/Bugfix-Issue-1712-sibling-issuetrackers-unguarded-cfg-cast.md` + wiki page.
  Out-of-scope same-family sites (githubrest/gitlabrest/kaitenrest/trellorest/jiradb) noted for
  follow-up. (Refs #1712)

- [KEY BUGFIX] - #1870: **both agent rulebooks told agents to recover a rejected push with
  `git rebase -X theirs origin/<your-branch>`** (`ai/FIX-ISSUE.md:134`, `ai/IMPLEMENT-TASK.md:139`)
  — in a rebase `theirs` is the REPLAYED (stale, agent-local) copy, so every overlap with a
  concurrent agent's push resolved toward the stale side and the retried push shipped the clobber
  as a clean fast-forward (re-measured this run on the 2-strategy harness: `-X theirs` → 0/45 live
  lines kept, `-X ours` → 45/45, both exit 0). Same cross-run data-loss class as #1694/#1868,
  affecting every shared file `.gitattributes merge=union` does not protect (`tmp/wiki-repo/`,
  `docs/`, the 10 i18n bundles). Fix (2 files, single-token swap + 4-line rationale): both lines now
  advise `git rebase -X ours` — upstream = the live `origin/<your-branch>` = ground truth. Verified:
  `grep -rn "rebase -X theirs" ai/` → 0 hits; regression suite `Regression — Issue #1870` PASS;
  no application code touched (Event Viewer n/a). Docs: `docs/Bugfix-Issue-1870-*.md` +
  wiki page; the sibling `docs/Bugfix-Issue-1868-*.md` mirror was missing and is now added.
  Discovered en route: #1868's workflow-side fix never actually landed (8 `-X theirs` sites still
  live in `.github/workflows/`, its commits exist in no ref despite the auto-close) → filed as
  **#1872** (`bug`). (Refs #1870)

- [KEY BUGFIX] - #1869: **on requirements-only projects (0 test cases) the simple Full-Text
  Search screen (`searchMgmt.html`) never showed the Req.Spec/Requirement result blocks even
  though the BFF returned them** — `api/searchmgmt/index.php` emitted
  `warning=empty_testproject` from a test-case-only flag (`getTestCaseIDSet()`), producing a
  self-contradictory payload (`warning=empty_testproject` + `count=4` + populated
  `reqspecs[]`/`requirements[]`), and `searchMgmt.html:352-363`'s early-return on that
  warning discarded the rows. Legacy `lib/search/search.php:145,156,171` cleared the warning
  whenever any result table was built, so legacy full-text search DID show reqspec hits on
  requirements-only projects. Fix (1 file): the BFF warning is now gated on the whole result
  set — `if ($total == 0) { $warning = $emptyTestProject ? 'empty_testproject' : 'no_records_found'; }`
  — so `empty_testproject` is only emitted when there is truly nothing to show; no client
  change was needed (the existing early-return then fires only when `total==0`). The sibling
  pattern in `api/search/index.php` was left untouched: its consumers show a warnBox
  *alongside* the rows (no results lost) and it had no symptom. Browser+curl verified on
  fixture project 9106 (REQONLY1869, requirements-enabled via the serialized
  `testprojects.options` blob — the legacy `option_reqs` column alone does not flip
  `reqEnabled` in `getOptions()`): BFF `{warning:"", count:4, rs:2, rq:2}`; browser renders
  "4 match(es)" with both Req.Spec (hrefs `reqSpecView.html?id=`, #1865 contract intact)
  and Requirement blocks; regression matrix 7 cases PASS (no-match notice paths,
  `no_records_found` on projects with TCs, requirements-disabled project, #1865
  click-through); Event Viewer: 0 new rows from the search flow; `php -l` clean; console
  clean. Regression suite "Regression — Issue #1869" 10/10 PASS, gate exit 0.
  Docs: `docs/Bugfix-Issue-1869-SearchMgmt-Empty-Testproject-Hides-ReqSpec-Results.md`.
  (Refs #1869)

- [KEY BUGFIX] - #1865: **the simple Full-Text Search screen (`searchMgmt.html`) linked every
  Requirement Specification result to `reqSpecView.html?reqspec_id=<id>`, but the viewer only
  resolved `id`/`req_spec_id` (`reqSpecView.html:310`) — `SPEC_ID` stayed 0 and 100% of RS
  results opened the "requirement specification does not exist or has been deleted" banner.**
  The legacy `openLinkedReqSpecWindow()` (`testlink_library.js:1166`) and every other modern
  producer emit the documented `id=` contract (`docs/WIKI-REQUIREMENT-SPEC-VIEWER.md`); the
  simple-search port was written against `reqspec_id` — the legacy PHP argument name of a
  *different* endpoint (`reqSpecPrint.php`). Fix (`3401c66a1`, 2 files): `searchMgmt.html:387`
  now emits `id=`, and `reqSpecView.html:310` additionally accepts `reqspec_id=` as a third
  alias so historical/bookmarked deep links keep working (primary names keep priority —
  `?reqspec_id=…&req_spec_id=…` resolves to `req_spec_id`). Browser-verified on fixture
  project 9096 (specs 9097/9098): DOM hrefs now `id=`, click-through loads the spec
  (`#deletedBanner` `display:none`, title+doc_id present), alias + `req_spec_id=` + `id=`
  all load, missing-id still shows `rsv.noId`, API `spec_view` contract unchanged, 0 new
  Event Viewer rows; code-review subagent APPROVE (XSS clean — `req_spec_id` is `intval()` at
  `api/search/index.php:604`). Regression suite "Regression — Issue #1865" 12/12 PASS, gate
  exit 0. Three sibling dead-link / empty-project defects found while reproducing were filed,
  not fixed: **#1866** (`suiteView.html?tsuite_id=` ignored by `suiteView.html:341`),
  **#1867** (`reqView.html?req_id=` ignored by `reqView.html:337`), **#1869**
  (`empty_testproject` early-return `searchMgmt.html:352-363` hides reqspec/requirement
  results on requirements-only projects). (Refs #1865)

- [KEY BUGFIX] - #1859: **legacy `lib/testcases/tcEdit.php` answered HTTP 500 with 0 bytes for any
  deep link without `tcversion_id` when the test case has no active version** (all `tcversions.active = 0`)
  or the id does not exist — `init_args()` ran `$nu = key($tcaseMgr->get_last_active_version($tcase_id))`
  on **every** request (`tcEdit.php:327`), and `get_last_active_version()` returns **null** for a 0-row
  result (`testcase.class.php:6182` + `database.class.php:666` `fetchRowsIntoMap()` keeps `$items = null`),
  so `key(null)` was an uncaught PHP 8 `TypeError` (no `events` row, only the server log). The line is
  dead code inherited from upstream 1.9.18 (`$nu` never read; `tcversion_id` legitimately stays `0` =
  `testcase::ALL_VERSIONS`). Fix: the same null-guard family used for this call at
  `requirement_spec_mgr.class.php:2639/2763` (`(array)` cast) and `specview.php:871`/`xmlrpc.class.php:6461`
  (`is_null()`) — an explicit `is_array($lastActiveVersion)` guard before `key()` (matches
  `api/reqtcassign/index.php:438`), null-safe `$nu`. Verified `bash tmp/verify_1859.sh` **PASS=9 FAIL=0**:
  no-doAction 200, `edit_tc` renders the no-active test case, absent id 200, active control unchanged,
  deactivate-last-version workflow 200, no new Error events / no new `tcEdit.php:327` TypeError. Regression
  suite "Regression — Issue #1859" appended to `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md` (7/7 PASS), gate exit 0.
  Five sibling latent defects discovered while testing were filed, not fixed: **#1860** (activate/deactivate
  /create-version render 500, Smarty `attachments.inc.tpl:106`), **#1861** (`requirement_mgr.class.php:1119`
  `current()` null), **#1862** (`testcase.class.php:5105` `count(null)` for the edit action on an absent id),
  **#1863** (4 `E_WARNING` from the `buildDirectWebLink()` `list()` destructure for absent ids),
  **#1864** (`testcase::addRelation()` writes `source_id=0` into `testcase_relations` when the source has no
  active version; verified repro in review, `testcase.class.php:8199-8200`). (Refs #1859)

- [NEW FEATURE] - #1095: **check/uncheck-all toggle per checkbox group** in the Advanced Search
  criteria form (`gui/templates/search/searchAdvancedView.html`), porting the legacy
  `toggle_all` icon + `cs_all_checkbox_in_div()` behavior
  (`searchGUI.inc.tpl:59-61,76-78,86-88,97-99`, `gui/javascript/checkboxes.js:244`).
  Each of the four attribute groups (Test Cases / Test Suites / Req. Specification / Requirement)
  now carries a master checkbox in its header that checks or unchecks every field of that group
  and mirrors the real group state (checked / **indeterminate** when partial), re-synced on every
  individual change and after *Reset*; the legacy `mm*Cell` hidden memory inputs are not needed
  because the modern master is derived from the actual checkboxes (same pattern as
  `reqTcBulkAssign.html:229-230`). i18n: `searchAdv.checkUncheckAll` added to all 10 client
  bundles (wired via `data-i18n-title`). No BFF change was required - the search keys
  (`tc_*`/`ts_*`/`rs_*`/`rq_*`) and `doSearch()` already handled all fields; the master ids use
  the `all_*` prefix so they are never submitted. Verified 14/14 PASS (toggle, indeterminate,
  reset, locale switch, search regression, Event Viewer clean); pre-existing console bug found
  while testing and filed, not fixed: **#1856**.

- [NEW FEATURE] - #1096: **Advanced Search result click on a Requirement Specification now opens
  THAT specification** (`gui/templates/search/searchAdvancedView.html:468` +
  `:545-553`). The previous handler `openReqSpecEdit(rsId)` received the spec id from the BFF
  result row and then ignored it, always loading the generic `reqSpecMgmt.html?tproject_id=…`
  management grid; the legacy screen opened the specific specification through
  `openLinkedReqSpecWindow()` (`lib/search/search.php:316` →
  `gui/javascript/testlink_library.js:1156-1166` → `reqSpecView.html?id=<req_spec_id>`).
  Renamed the handler to `openReqSpecView()` (it no longer edits anything) and it now builds
  `reqSpecView.html?id=<rsId>&tproject_id=<tprojectId>`, the same popup shape as the sibling
  `openTcEdit`/`openTsEdit`/`openReqEdit` handlers. No BFF change was needed (`api/search/index.php:604`
  already returned `req_spec_id`) and no new i18n keys (no user-facing strings). Verified 11/11 PASS
  (test suite "Task — Issue #1096" in `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md`): each result row opens its own spec,
  TC/suite links regression-checked, i18n coverage gate green, Event Viewer clean; two defects found
  while testing were filed separately: **#1865** (`searchMgmt.html` RS links use the unread
  `reqspec_id=` parameter) and pre-existing **#1856** (console `ReferenceError: p`). (Refs #1096)

- [NEW FEATURE] - #1097: **Advanced Search deep links with a URL `target` param now
  auto-submit on load** (legacy `forceSearch` parity). Legacy
  `lib/search/searchMgmt.php:99` computed `forceSearch = strlen(trim($args->target)) > 0`
  and `dashio/search/searchGUI.inc.tpl:257-259` submitted the form on
  jQuery/onload; the modern `searchAdvancedView.html` only *prefilled* the URL params - and even
  that was broken, because `var p = new URLSearchParams(...)` was declared inside the
  jQuery-ready closure while the global `loadContext()` reads it, so the prefill block threw
  `ReferenceError: p is not defined` (bug **#1856**) and no results ever loaded. Fix (1 file,
  `gui/templates/search/searchAdvancedView.html`): `p` is now global (`searchMgmt.html:154`
  pattern) and, right after the URL prefill, `if ($.trim(p.get('target') || '') !== '') { doSearch(); }`
  mirrors legacy forceSearch exactly - deep links (bookmarked searches, navBar one-box hand-off)
  land on results with no Find click. No BFF change and no new i18n keys (`action=fulltext`
  already accepts `target`); a deep link *without* `target` keeps the bare-form behaviour
  (0 `action=fulltext` requests). Verified in-browser (fixture project 1 "Search Gap Demo",
  2 TCs): deep link prefills + auto-fires `action=fulltext` + renders 1 match, console zero
  errors (ReferenceError gone), manual Find/Reset regression OK, sibling `searchMgmt.html`
  navBar hand-off regression OK, test suite "Task — Issue #1097" 10/10 PASS, i18n coverage
  gate green, Event Viewer clean. (Refs #1097, Fixes #1856)

