- [MODERNIZED SCREEN] - #1871: **Platform Create/Edit** (`lib/platforms/platformsEdit.php` ->
  `gui/templates/platforms/platformsEdit.html` + `api/platformedit/index.php`): the legacy Smarty
  create/edit form is now a standalone Dashio screen (mode cards, name/notes, the three legacy
  flags, delete-confirm modal, localized state cards) behind a session-authenticated BFF that
  re-checks `platform_view`/`platform_management` on the OWNING project, pre-checks duplicate
  names on create AND update (ownership proven before the name probe), blocks deletion with
  `422 DELETE_BLOCKED` while the platform is linked to a test plan, and refuses wrong verbs
  (405) and cross-origin POSTs (403 CSRF). Legacy controller kept as a session-guarded
  GET/HEAD-only 302 shim. Four defects found while testing and fixed in the same run:
  raw `-4` duplicate code on create, the shim answering 302 to POST, a stale MODE card after
  create, and a missing Dashio Bootstrap JS include that left the delete modal dead.
  Code review additionally moved the session gate before the DB connect, made `init`
  check rights before resolving the project (uniform 403, no existence oracle) and added
  a server-side 100-char name cap.
  (Refs #1871)

- [MODERNIZED SCREEN] - #1845: **Priority Bar Chart** is no longer a dead endpoint.
  Legacy `lib/results/priorityBarChart.php` was **unreachable fatal code** on 2.0.1: it
  required `third_party/charts/charts.php` and `lib/functions/results.class.php`, both gone
  since the phpchart drop, so every request answered HTTP 500 with an empty body - and it
  performed **no rights check at all**, so any authenticated user could read the per-keyword
  result breakdown of any test plan (`$tplan_id` came raw out of `$_REQUEST`, and the
  `$tproject_id` assertion was never compared with the plan's real owner). New BFF
  `api/prioritybarchart/index.php` (`action=init`, session + same-origin guarded,
  `testplan_metrics` right on the **owning** project, owning-plan resolution, 400/401/403/
  404/405 JSON contract) + new Dashio screen `gui/templates/results/priorityBarChart.html`
  (stacked pass/failed/blocked/not-run bars per keyword, DataTable, CSV export, localized
  empty/denied/mismatch/error states) reachable from the *Results by Keyword* section of
  `gui/templates/results/charts.html` and from `$actions->priorityBarChart`
  (`lib/functions/common.php`). The unit counted is the test-case version assigned to the
  plan, each version lands in exactly one bucket decided by its latest execution row, and the
  raw execution-row count is reported separately. i18n: 46 `pbc.*` keys + 1 footer key in all
  10 client bundles. The legacy URL is now a launcher shim (302 for browsers, 405
  `modern_endpoint_only` for XHR callers). **3 bugs filed + fixed** while building and
  reviewing it: **#1846** the first BFF commit called `fetchFirstRowSingleColumn()` with
  1 argument instead of 2, so every request answered 500 with an empty body; **#1847**
  `bar()` composed its label key from the CSS class and the grey segment's tooltip
  rendered the raw key `pbc.seriesNot_run` (the bundle key is `pbc.seriesNotRun` and
  `TLi18n.t()` has no fallback); **#1848** the unknown-failure branch fed the BFF message
  to `TLi18n.t()`, printing an English server string inside a localized card while
  `pbc.serverErrorBody` stayed dead. The mandatory code review additionally fixed the
  `tproject_id` assertion running before the rights check (an IDOR probe),
  `platform_id = 0` counted as a real platform, a redundant `GROUP BY`/`COUNT(*)` in the
  latest-result query, a duplicated version map and unquoted CSV cells.

- [NEW FEATURE] - #1277 (ISTQB #1054): **Risk-Based Testing** module implemented from scratch -
  new BFF `api/riskcoverage/index.php` + new Dashio screen
  `gui/templates/results/riskCoverage.html`, reachable from Metrics & Reports
  (`risk_coverage` report entry, `cfg/reports.cfg.php` + `api/resultsnav/index.php:164`).
  Adds the ISTQB likelihood(1-5) x impact(1-5) risk model on test cases (score 1..25, levels
  low/medium/high in a lazily created `tc_risk` table), a **requirement risk-coverage view**
  (covered / not tested / uncovered requirements against max+avg+residual risk), an editable
  **test case risk register** with a live 5x5 risk matrix modal, and **metrics grouped by risk
  level with a risk-level filter**. Unrated test cases fall back to the 1.9.20 importance x
  urgency proxy. i18n: 74 `risk.*` keys in all 10 client bundles + `link_report_risk_coverage`
  in all 19 locale strings files. AUDIT events emitted on every rating save.

- [FEATURE GAP CLOSED] - #1262: the **Free Test Cases report regained full legacy
