- [KEY BUGFIX] (security) - #1808: **the read-only Execution Notes fragment is now same-origin on
  BOTH of the entry points that produce it.** The #1807 fix had closed the IDOR and the stored
  RichEdit XSS, but `api/execnotesreadonly/index.php` exposes `?action=fragment` as a public route
  whose whole purpose is the legacy `url2load()` contract, and that fragment is assigned into
  `innerHTML` by 5 legacy templates. Its same-origin requirement lived ONLY inside the shim
  `lib/execute/getExecNotes.php`, so the same request against the BFF's own documented fragment
  route answered **200 + the notes** with `Origin: http://evil.example` while the shim answered 403
  for byte-identical output - the security property depended on which URL a caller happened to use.
  Root cause: `bffSameOriginGuard()` (`api/_guard.php:102-106`) returns immediately for
  GET/HEAD/OPTIONS, so on this read-only endpoint - where `enro_require_safe_verb()` has already
  restricted the verb set - it was structurally unreachable. New `enro_require_same_origin_fragment()`
  in the BFF follows the shared guard's semantics (`api/_guard.php:126-145`, which the shim mirrors
  and is slightly STRICTER than - it requires EVERY present header to match while this one returns on
  the first match; the only divergent combination is a same-origin `Origin` paired with a foreign
  `Referer`, where the shim runs first and is the stricter one, so the effective verdict never changes
  and no legacy call site can break), scoped to `action=fragment` only: a
  PRESENT `Origin`/`Referer` is authoritative (unparseable -> 403 `unparseable_origin`, foreign ->
  403 `cross_origin`, and the `X-Requested-With` hint never overrides it, issue #1679), neither
  header -> the XRW fallback that a same-origin `$.ajax` sends, otherwise 403. It runs before the
  user row is resolved and before `bffEnforceSession()`, so a foreign caller learns nothing and
  cannot keep a stale session alive. `action=view` is deliberately NOT gated: it is JSON, its only
  caller is the same-origin `$.getJSON` in `execNotesReadonly.html:169`, and the endpoint sends no
  `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`. Verified: the 8-case origin matrix passes 8/8, and all 15 status
  codes of the pre-existing rights / id-validation / no-session / POST / 302 probes are byte-for-byte
  unchanged (captured before and after); in headless Chrome the stored
  `<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>` + `<script>` payload arrives as ONE text node with 0 injected
  elements and no console errors; `events` gained no Error/Warning row (refusals are logged AUDIT).
  Also from the mandatory code review (subagent, **no blockers**): `?action[]=fragment` and
  `?exec_id[]=1` reached the `(string)` cast and emitted "Array to string conversion" as an E_WARNING -
  which `watchPHPErrors()` (`lib/functions/logger.class.php:1483`) writes into the EVENTS TABLE, and
  **unauthenticated**, because the parse runs before the session check, so any anonymous caller could
  add a Warning to the Event Viewer; both parameters are now `is_scalar()`-guarded and a non-scalar is
  normalised onto the invalid-parameter path (400) with no warning. The new refusal helper also gained
  the `headers_sent()` guard its siblings `enro_fail()` / `bffRejectForbidden()` have, so a refusal can
  never degrade into a 200 should the bootstrap ever emit output first. Suite `Issue #1808` in
  `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md`.

