- [TASK] - #1288: **The first computer bug (9 September 1947) is now documented.** The corpus
  never explained where the word *bug* that names this product's whole category comes from: the
  `Istoric` section of the wiki landing page (`tmp/wiki-repo/Ce-este-TestLink.md`) started at
  "Lansat: 2004 - SourceForge" and `grep -rniE "1947|Mark II|moth|Hopper" docs/ tmp/wiki-repo/*.md
  README.md CHANGELOG --include=*.md` returned **0 hits in 1277 markdown files**. New wiki page
  **[Prima Bug din Istorie](https://github.com/sebiboga/testlink-upgraded/wiki/Prima-Bug-Istorica)**
  (9 sections, Romanian, the wiki language) tells the incident - the moth taped into the Harvard
  Mark II operating log by Grace Hopper's team - and, more importantly for QA, what came *after*
  the moth: isolation to a single relay, verification of every screw, a screw not tightened to
  ground as the actual cause, ~69 hours to full return to service - i.e. observe -> document ->
  diagnose -> repair -> retest, the discipline TestLink implements today. It also states the
  nuance the issue title glosses over: the word predates the moth (Edison, ~1878; *buggy*,
  *glitch*), so the page claims only the **first documented** computer bug. Sections map the era to
  2.0.1 (punched cards -> `api/**` BFF, paper operating log -> `events` table behind the Event
  Viewer, hardware bug -> custom fields + execution status) and end with a 5-step "how to log a
  real bug in TestLink" recipe. Cross-linked: `Ce-este-TestLink.md` history section (new first
  entry), `Home.md` index (item 32 + the page-count heading corrected `31 Pagini` -> `32 Pagini`) and
  the Features Coverage table; English mirror without image lines at `docs/first-bug-1947.md`.
  Illustration: Event Viewer screenshot (the mark-II log book's descendant) committed to the wiki
  as `issue-1288-eventviewer-audit-trail.png`. No screen, BFF, DB or i18n change. (Refs #1288)

