  persisted them with `cfield_mgr->design_values_to_db($_REQUEST, $buildID, $cf_map, null,
  'build')`, but the modern inline Create/Edit modal of `buildsView.html` never grew the CF block
  and the BFF ignored them entirely - so build custom fields were a **silent drop on both halves**:
  the definitions were neither shown nor written. New `GET /api/builds/index.php/cfields?tplan_id=N
  [&build_id=M]` returns them as **DATA** (never HTML, so a free-text CF label/possible value can
  never inject markup; the owning project is proven BEFORE the build is resolved, and a build
  outside the addressed project is a 404, never a silent read of another project's values), and
  `POST /` + `PUT /{id}` rebuild the legacy `custom_field_<type>_<id>` hash from the field ids **the
  server resolved**, so a submitted key can never name a field outside the project. BFF defects
  found and fixed while testing: (a) a date CF is stored as a UNIX timestamp (`mktime` in
  `_build_cfield`) but the write path fed ISO straight into `split_localized_date()`, which parses
  the **session locale** format (`d/m/Y` for en_GB, `m/d/Y` for en_US, `d.m.Y` for de_DE, ...) -
  so the same ISO input was stored as a **different calendar day per locale** (measured:
  `2026-11-15` became **2021-05-18** under en_GB); the client keeps speaking ISO and the server now
  owns the locale conversion (`epochToIsoDate()` / `isoToLocaleDate()`), verified round trip
  identical for en_GB/en_US/ja_JP/de_DE. (b) `design_values_to_db()` writes **every** field of the
  passed `$cfMap` (the hash only supplies values), so a partial `PUT` silently cleared the rest
  while `cfields_written` reported the submitted count - the full-replacement legacy semantics are
  now explicit and the reported count matches what was written. (c) `GET/PUT/DELETE /{id}` and
  `/{id}/flags` accepted a `tplan_id` and then **ignored** it (`resolveBuild()` derives the project
  from `build.testproject_id`, so the RIGHT was checked correctly but the ADDRESS was not) - a
  stale or mis-scoped page could rename or **DELETE** a build of another project and see the result
  inside this plan's context (measured: cross-project `DELETE` returned 200 and deleted the build);
  now a build addressed through a foreign plan is a 404. (d) `rights.canViewEvents`
  (`mgt_view_events`) was never in the payload, so the event history button could not show.
  Seven more defects were found by the mandatory code review of the finished screen: (e) the CF timestamp was
  read back with `gmdate()` although `_build_cfield()` stores it with `mktime()` (LOCAL
  midnight), which agreed by accident on the UTC CI host and silently returned the **previous
  day** on every east-of-UTC install (measured with `TZ=Europe/Bucharest`: a typed
  `2026-11-15` was stored as `1794693600` and read back as **2026-11-14**; same for
  `Asia/Tokyo`) - `date()` reads it back identically in every zone probed; (f) the screen
  addressed its own build with `GET /{id}` **without** `tplan_id`, so the cross-project check
  above did not apply to the screen's own prefill; (g) a **datetime (type 10)** CF rendered as
  a plain text box and the write path pinned `custom_field_10_<id>_hour/_minute/_second` to `0`,
  silently reducing it to midnight - it now renders `<input type="datetime-local">` and the
  submitted time of day reaches the stamp.
  `lib/plan/buildEdit.php` also no longer fatals with `Call to undefined method
  build::getCustomFieldsValues()` (a method removed in 2.0.1 but still called at
  `buildView.php:94`, `planView.php:75`). Four of the review findings were **blockers or data loss**: (h)
  the shim's `redirect($target, 'window.location.replace')` built `window.location.replace.href='...'`
  (`redirect()` concatenates `$level . '.href'`), i.e. it assigned an expando to the function object and the
  bookmark landed on a **blank page** - the replacement is now emitted directly; (i) `saveBuildCfields()` ran on
  every `PUT` and `design_values_to_db()` writes **every** field of `$cfMap`, so an **inline rename from
