  answering `cfields_written: N` - the write is now gated on the key being present, which keeps full
  replacement for the full-screen editor and leaves the table's modal alone; (j) `POST /{id}/flags` read
  `tplan_id` only from the **query**, while `buildsView.html` sends it in the **JSON body**, so the
  Active/Open toggles were not covered by the new scope check; (k) the audit string read `$ctx['tplan_name']`
  on a `resolveBuild()` context that has no such key, logging `Undefined array key` and an empty plan name on
  **every build save** (measured `E_WARNING` in the Event Viewer) - and `required` was read from a
  non-existent `values_required` column instead of `cfield_testprojects.required`, so the red mandatory `*` could
  never appear; an unchecked checkbox/multiselection also stored NULL through `$value[0]` on an empty array
  (`E_WARNING` + two deprecations), and the #1788 fatal fix itself had turned the fatal into
  `Undefined array key "input"` - all fixed. i18n: 51 `bedit.*` +
  `bv.createBuildFullScreen` + `footers.buildEdit` in **all 10** bundles, appended as text so each
  bundle's existing formatting/ordering is untouched and a concurrent CI agent is never
  reformatted away. 26/26 test cases PASS (23 functional + 3 from the code review), console and Event Viewer
  clean. (Refs #1787)

- [KEY BUGFIX - DATA INTEGRITY] - #1684: `reqTreeReorder.html` - the per-row **Up / Down / To top / To bottom**
  buttons reordered the **SELECTED** requirement instead of the row whose button was clicked, silently corrupting
  the pending order that **Apply** then writes to the database. Root cause was a shared-state collision, not a
  missing argument: `PICKED` (`reqTreeReorder.html:168` pre-fix / `:173` now, "requirement id chosen in the Move card") did double duty
  as the move-card selection **and** as the implicit row resolver - `btn()` (`:283-285` pre-fix) forwarded only the direction,
  dropping the row index `i` that the enclosing `ITEMS.forEach(function (it, i))` loop supplied, and `nudge()`
  (`:289-291` pre-fix) recovered the row with `ITEMS.findIndex(function (x) { return x.id === PICKED; })`. The smell is
  provable from the source alone: `applyRowState()` (`:225-228` pre-fix / `:256-259` now) already disabled
  the controls **per row**
  (`i === 0` for up/top, `i === n - 1` for down/bottom), so the markup advertised row-scoped controls while the
  handler was selection-scoped. Two silent variants, both reproduced: select row 2 + **To top** on row 3 gave
  `TR1-3, TR1-1, TR1-2` instead of `TR1-2, TR1-1, TR1-3` (and **Apply** persisted exactly that wrong order), and
  select row 1 + **Up** on row 3 changed nothing at all because `j < 0` bailed out with no message. Measured as
  0 console errors/warnings and **0 XHRs** during the faulty clicks, so the BFF was never in the fault path - the
  `api/reqtreereorder/index.php` reorder endpoint (`?action=reorder`, wired at `reqTreeReorder.html:169`) needed no
  change. Fix (commit `f60e8965d`, landed with the #1681
  screen series and verified + closed by this run): `btn(icon, label, dir, idx)` binds the row it is rendered for
  and calls `nudge(idx, dir)`; `nudge(i, dir)` works purely on that bounds-validated index, and the `PICKED`
  lookup plus the "first enabled button" fallback are **deleted**, making the invariant a property of the
  signature - a reorder control can no longer reach the selection. Safe because every reorder ends in `render()`,
  which rebuilds all handlers with fresh indices. 1 file, +10/-14. Regression suite 1684: **9/9 PASS**, including
  the Apply -> `nodes_hierarchy.node_order` round trip that now stores the **clicked** row's order. A DOM-vs-handler
  mismatch grep is documented on the wiki page for the next screen that mixes per-row controls with a shared
  selection. Filed as #1804, later fixed there (see the #1804 entry at the top): the disabled
  controls were `<span class="rm dis">` rather than real `<button disabled>`, so they lacked
  `aria-disabled` semantics, `pointer-events:none` and a "why" tooltip.
  (Fixes #1684)

- [KEY BUGFIX] - #1683: `reqTreeReorder.html` fell back to a **native `alert()`** for EVERY confirm dialog
