  destructive actions**, purely client-side, no `api/` code and no data-integrity exposure. This run found the
  fix already on `origin/sebiboga` and verified it end-to-end rather than re-doing it: Move and Apply dialogs are
  real BS3 modals (`class="modal fade in"` + `.modal-backdrop` at `opacity 0.5`, no DevTools JS dialog raised),
  the close button is `<button class="close" data-dismiss="modal">&times;</button>`, Cancel hides the modal and
  writes nothing, OK persists (`TR1-3` moved `srs_id 2 -> 4`; order saved, banner "The new order was saved."),
  console clean, Event Viewer `log_level IN (1,2)` = 0. Regression suite 1683: **12/12 PASS**. Also filed
  **#1796** from the repo-wide grep the report asked for: three screens still carry **dead** BS4/5 *CSS* classes
