- [KEY BUGFIX] - #1689: `reqTreeReorder.html` showed a **fully working drag affordance to read-only users** -
  `draggable="true"` on every row - while every drop was silently discarded. `render()` gated the attribute on
  `GRANT.modify && !DEAD`, but `render()` ends by calling `applyRowState()`, which re-wrote the same attribute
  from a weaker `DEAD`-only predicate (`gui/templates/requirements/reqTreeReorder.html:272`, pre-fix), so the
  weaker copy always won; `dragstart` fired and `dragover` was `defaultPrevented`, so the browser painted a
  live drop target that the `drop` guard (`:329`, `if (DEAD || !GRANT.modify || BUSY) return;`) then ignored.
  Introduced by `13b53dd94` (the #1688 fix), which folded `DEAD` into the row controls but dropped the rights
  term that the #1681 branch had put in `render()` - so #1689 had been fixed and then regressed, and the
  regression passed review because its non-regression was measured only for a user WITH modify rights. Fix: a
  single `canDrag()` predicate (`!DEAD && !!GRANT.modify`) that both writers call, so the affordance is derived
  from the capability the `drop` handler enforces and the next rights term cannot be missed again. Measured:
  view-only 3/3 rows `draggable=true -> false` (drag now offers no gesture at all), the admin path unchanged and
  still persisting (`action=init` serverOrder `[8,6,10]`), and both #1688 DEAD paths - including the
  success -> dead transition with surviving rows - still forcing `draggable=false`. 0 new Event Viewer rows.
  (Fixes #1689)
- [KEY BUGFIX] - #1824: `reqTreeReorder.html` kept **both reordering affordances live while an Apply/Move
  request was in flight**, although every handler refused on `BUSY`. Same defect class as #1689 (a capability
  predicate written per control and left to drift), pre-existing - the two weaker copies are byte-identical
  before `4c8b3a62b` and were deliberately left out of that commit. Root cause, two hops:
  (1) `canDrag()` (`:259-261`) mirrored only `DEAD` + rights, so `draggable` (`:290`, `:311`), the grip (`:291`,
  `:315`) and the `dragover` `preventDefault()` (`:349`, the call that paints a row as a legal drop target)
  kept advertising a gesture the `drop` guard (`:341`) refused; (2) the arrow buttons are created as
