- [KEY BUGFIX - SECURITY] - #1792: `api/builds/index.php` resolved the addressed test plan BEFORE it
  checked rights, so a user with **no rights at all** (role_id 3) got a different status for a plan
  that EXISTS than for one that does not - and the status alone therefore enumerated every test plan
  id in the installation. `resolveTplan()` (`:67`) answered `404 "Invalid Test Plan ID"` for an absent
  id while `canManage()` (`:142`) answered `403 "Insufficient rights"` for a present one, and the 403
  was reachable only when the row was there. Measured live on a fresh DB (private project 9018, plan
  9019, build 1, user `sm1792norights`): the 403/404 split existed on **six** route families
  (`GET /`, `GET /cfields`, `POST /`, `PUT /{id}`, `POST /{id}/flags`, `DELETE /{id}`) - two more than
  reported, because `assertBuildInTplan()` carried the same inversion - and the `build_id` axis split
  too (`GET /{id}`: 403 vs `404 "Build not found"`), contradicting the code comment at `:115` that
  claimed it was already clean. Fix: **collapse** rather than reorder. These routes derive the owning
  project FROM the addressed row, so - unlike `api/plans/index.php:127-131`, which can ask
  `canManage()` about a project the caller named - there is nothing to check rights against before the
  lookup, and reordering is not available. Two helpers now carry every refusal of each family:
  `outPlanNotFound()` (`404 "Invalid Test Plan ID"`) for the plan-addressed routes and
  `outBuildNotFound()` (`404 "Build not found"` + `error_code: build_not_found`) for the
  build-addressed ones, wired into all 7 handlers plus `resolveTplan()` and `assertBuildInTplan()`;
  `resolveTplanGated()` fuses `resolveTplan()` + `canManage()` so the three plan routes can no longer
  express the split. "Absent", "belongs to another project" and "you may not manage it" are now
  byte-identical, so no route can distinguish them. The `tplan_id=0` project-scoped list deliberately
  KEEPS its 403 - its project comes from `$_SESSION['testprojectID']`, not from the caller, so nothing
  is concealed. `resolveBuild()` no longer emits a THIRD body ("Invalid Test Project ID") when a
  build's owner no longer resolves - it fails through the caller's family. Code review also found
  two client defects this exposed: `buildEdit.html`'s `errText()` keyed `'Invalid test plan id'`
  while the server emits `'Invalid Test Plan ID'` (case-sensitive, so it never matched and the raw
  English reached the DOM), and `buildsView.html` had no mapping for `'Build not found'` at all;
  both now map to keys that already exist in all 10 locale bundles, so no new i18n key was needed.
  Verified: no over-blocking - `admin` still gets 200 + the plan context on all six legs and still
  gets an honest 404 for a genuinely absent plan; 69/69 regression assertions PASS
  (`tmp/verify_1792.php`, which fails 22 of them against the pre-patch file), Event Viewer 0 new
  ERROR/WARNING, `php -l` clean. Residual: a timing side channel survives, and the dangling-owner
  branch was not provably reachable pre-patch (documented in docs/). (Fixes #1792)
