- [KEY BUGFIX] - #1648: `GET /api/tcassignments/index.php/rows` answered **HTTP 500 with a 0-byte
  body** (`TypeError: array_keys(): Argument #1 ($array) must be of type array, null given` at
  `api/tcassignments/index.php:348` pre-fix) on every request without assignments - i.e. on the modernized
  **My Test Case Assignments** screen for any test project that has no test plan, which is every
  freshly imported installation. The value was assigned *inside* the row-building guard
  (`$statusCodes = $resultsCfg['status_code'];` at `:240` pre-fix) but consumed *outside* it
  (`'statusKeys' => array_keys($statusCodes)` at `:348` pre-fix); both lines came from the same commit
  `023e60cedb` (Refs #660), and the bug was invisible because the only consumer sits on the
  success payload. `get_assigned_to_user()` returns NULL for "no assignments" (legacy parity), so
  the guard skipped the assignment and `array_keys(null)` killed the request; PHP additionally
  emitted `Undefined variable $statusCodes` first, writing one spurious `log_level=2` Event Viewer
  warning per failed load. Fix: hoist the read above the guard with a defensive cast
  (`$statusCodes = (array)($resultsCfg['status_code'] ?? []);`), which also keeps the documented
  `statusKeys` payload field complete in the empty case - the issue's suggested
  `is_array(...) ? array_keys(...) : []` at `:348` was rejected because it silently empties that
  field. No frontend/i18n change (`statusKeys` currently has no consumer in `gui/`; the screen maps
  each row's `status_key` through its own `statusLabel()` map). Verified: empty-plan project now
  `HTTP=200` with `groups: []` + all 7 status keys (`all` is the filter sentinel among them),
  populated-project payload byte-identical, 401/403/404/validation bodies unchanged, `quick_result`
  unaffected, Event Viewer delta 0 across 3 repeats, browser console clean and the screen now
  renders its "No test cases assigned." empty state. Pre-existing defect found while testing and
