 - [KEY BUGFIX] - #1701: a failed issue-tracker connection check recorded **no cause at all**, and the `502` fallback row named **no source**. Two independent defects on one code path. (A) `lib/issuetrackerintegration/issueTrackerInterface.class.php:222-223` built the log context with *simple* string interpolation (`"$this->cfg->dbhost - " . "DBName: $this->cfg->dbname ..."`), and PHP resolves only **one** property level in a non-curly interpolated string: it interpolated `$this->cfg` and left `->dbhost` as literal text. `$this->cfg` is a `stdClass` (deliberately - `setCfg()` `:165` does `json_decode(json_encode($this->cfg))` so the config can live in `$_SESSION`, a `SimpleXMLElement` not being serializable), and a `stdClass` has no `__toString`, so the statement raised `Error: Object of class stdClass could not be converted to string` (an `Error`, not a `TypeError`: the offending value is `$this->cfg`, whose type is unconstrained, and `catch (\Throwable)` catches it either way) and **aborted before the `tLog()` on the next line that records host / database / user / ADODB code** - i.e. the useful message was dead code and the only thing the Event Viewer ever held for a dead host was the language error. Isolated in 9 lines with no TestLink code: `"$a->cfg->dbhost"` on a `stdClass` throws identically. It only fires on the *failure* branch of `connect()`, so healthy trackers never showed it. (B) `api/issuetracker/index.php:217` and `:260` logged `tLog(__METHOD__ . ' ' . $e->getMessage(), 'ERROR')`; `__METHOD__` is `__CLASS__ :: __FUNCTION__` and at the **top level of a request script** there is neither, so in PHP 8 it expands to `""` and the row was a bare `" <message>"` - measured `LENGTH=58` with `HEX(LEFT(description,20))` = `204F626A656374206F6620636C61737320737464` (40 hex chars = 20 bytes), starting `20` (one ASCII space). Fix: curly-brace interpolation (`{$this->cfg->dbhost}`) so the intended string is built and the existing `tLog()` runs, plus an explicit liter