KEY BUGFIX / COMPATIBILITY EFFORTS (selection)
----------------------------------------------
- [KEY BUGFIX] - #1635: the vendored `third_party/phpxmlrpc/lib/xmlrpc.inc` (Trac XML-RPC
  issue-tracker transport) could not even be **compiled** on PHP 8: `$temp =& new xmlrpcval(...)`
  at `:554` assigns the result of `new` by reference, removed in PHP 7, so every request that
  transitively loaded it died with a compile-time `ParseError` -> **HTTP 500 with a 0-byte body
  and NO Event Viewer row** (a fatal never reaches `tLog()`). Measured blast radius, wider than
  the report: not only the *Check connection* wrench
  (`GET /api/issuetracker/index.php/{id}/check-connection`) and the modal *Check Connection*
  button, but the **Issue Trackers Management grid itself** (`GET /api/issuetracker/index.php`,
  because `tlIssueTracker::getAll()` resolves every row's implementation) rendered completely
  EMPTY as soon as one Trac/XML-RPC tracker existed, as did `GET /cfg-template?type=19`. Two
  stacked PHP-8 removals, one root cause (a PHP-4 era vendored library): the report's line 554
  was only the **first of 47** `=& new` sites (`php -l` stops at the first), and the 4
  PHP-4-style constructors (`xmlrpc_client`/`xmlrpcmsg`/`xmlrpcresp`/`xmlrpcval`) are no longer
  constructors, so `new xmlrpc_client($url)` silently returned an uninitialised object
  (measured `path=NULL server=NULL port=0`; after the fix `path='/trac/xmlrpc' server='127.0.0.1'
  port=9`). Fix: all 47 references dropped (object handles make `= new` equivalent) and the 4
  constructors renamed to `__construct`; plus defence in depth at the three places that
  autoload an implementation class: in `api/issuetracker/index.php` the `class_exists($impl)`
  probe sat **outside** the `try` of both check-connection routes (it now sits inside -> the
  route's existing logged 502 + Event Viewer ERROR row) and the `cfg-template` include got its
  own `try` (-> the structured `interface_missing` code), and in `tlIssueTracker::getAll()` the
  `@class_exists($impl)` probe of the per-row `checkEnv` guard is now inside a
  `try/catch(\Throwable)` that degrades that single row (the `@` cannot suppress a Throwable,
  so a broken file still blanked the whole grid). Measured with the library reverted again as a
  fault injection: grid `200` with the row still listed, check-connection `502`, cfg-template
  `200 interface_missing`, 3 Event Viewer ERROR rows - no 0-byte 500 on any of them. Regression suite 1635
  in `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md`: 14 PASS / 0 FAIL / 1 known residual - the wire layer below the
  client object still uses the removed `each()` (14 sites) and `split()` (1 site), so a real
  `ticket.get` round-trip still fatals; that port, plus the fact that
  `tracxmlrpcInterface::connect()` never probes the server and therefore answers
  `connected:true` for an unreachable host, is filed as a follow-up issue (Refs #1635).
- Reorder Requirements screen (`gui/templates/requirements/reqReorder.html`)
  linked Font Awesome from the Dashio-local copy
  (`/gui/templates/dashio/lib/font-awesome/css/all.min.css`), a FA 6 file that
  is never shipped (only FA 4 `font-awesome.min.css` exists in Dashio) → HTTP
  404 on every load and empty/tofu FA glyphs. Switched the `<link>` to the CDN
  URL (`https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css`)
  used by the other 148 modern screens; icon rendering + full reorder
  save/persist regression verified (Refs #1534).
- `linkto.php` inner-frame deep links (`item=reqspec|testcase|testsuite`) returned
  HTTP 500 on every hit: the inner-frame branch still called
  `testproject::setSessionProject()`, a method removed from
  `lib/functions/testproject.class.php` during the TN2023-97 refactor (commit
  `94c9adf5c`) → PHP 8 `Call to undefined method`. Replaced the call with direct
  `$_SESSION` assignment restoring the removed method's exact semantics
  (id/name/color/prefix + option_reqs/priority/automation) from the already-fetched
  `$tproject_data` row, so reqspec/testcase/testsuite bookmark links open the legacy
  tree+work frames again (`item=req` keeps the modern directLink resolver, #1532).
  Also re-added the missing legacy i18n key `testsuite_not_found` (a
  `log_level=32` LOCALIZATION Event Viewer warning on every testsuite deep link) to
  all 14 full locale bundles (Fixes #1533).
- `ltx.php` execution deep links (`item=exec`) returned HTTP 500 on every hit:
  `launch_inner_exec()` still called `testproject::setSessionProject()` at
  `ltx.php:334` — the same method removed during the TN2023-97 refactor (commit
  `94c9adf5c`, sibling of the #1533 linkto.php fatal) → PHP 8
  `Call to undefined method`. Replaced the call with direct `$_SESSION`
  assignment restoring the removed method's exact semantics (id/name/color/prefix
  + option_reqs/priority/automation) from the project row fetched via the already
  instantiated `$tproject_mgr`, so execution links from email notifications open
  the exec dashboard (execNavigator) again — inner (`feature_id`/3-key) and outer
  flows, plus the `xta2m` regression all verified (Fixes #1537; follow-up
  execSetResults workframe defect filed as #1538).
- `execSetResults.php` execution deep links still failed after #1537: the exec
  **workframe** URL built by `ltx.php process_exec()` (and by the modern
  assigned-tc links) carries **no form_token** and the settings under their
  cache-key names (`setting_testplan`/`setting_build`/`setting_platform`), but
  `getSettingsAndFilters()`'s form-tokenless fallback read the *prop* names
  (`tplan_id`/`build_id`/`platform_id`) → `tplan_id=0` → HTTP 500 `Bad Test
  Project ID` (`execSetResults.php:706`). The fallback now reads
  `$_REQUEST[$cacheKey]` (`setting_*`, and the `filter_*` cache keys) **first**
  and falls back to `$_REQUEST[$prop]` for the legacy `tplan_id` callers, so
  setting_* deep links, filter cache-key params and `tplan_id` links all render
  the execution pane again (regression from commit `857555dad`, which flipped
  the upstream `ff21e9920` `$_REQUEST[$sfKey]` behavior) (Fixes #1538).
- Stored XSS in the role-assignment screens (`usersAssignProject.html`,
  `usersAssignPlan.html`): DB-controlled project/plan/user/role display names
  were concatenated raw into `<option>`/`<td>` HTML, so a project named
  `<img src=x onerror=...>` executed on every page load. Added the `esc()`
  helper to `usersAssignPlan.html` (reused the one already present in
  `usersAssignProject.html`) and applied it to every DB-sourced interpolation
  (project/plan name, user login/name, role name, inheritedRoleName) plus the
