- BFF role creation: `POST /api/roles` with a `rightIDs` array containing `0`
  (or an empty/no rights payload) crashed with an uncaught PHP 8
  `TypeError: sizeof(): Argument #1 ... null given` in `tlRole::checkDetails()`
  — HTTP 500 with an empty body instead of the intended validation JSON.
  `checkDetails` now tests `empty($this->rights)` (null-safe, identical
  semantics for arrays), so invalid/no-right payloads reach the declared
  `E_EMPTYROLE` 400 branch "Role must have at least one right" (Fixes #1531).
- BFF role create/edit: `POST/PUT /api/roles` accepted nonexistent `rightIDs`
  (e.g. `[99999]`) and attached them, minting dangling `role_rights` rows shown
  as `{"id":99999,"name":null}` in the role list. `tlRight::_clean()` keeps
  `dbID` under `TLOBJ_O_SEARCH_BY_ID`, so the old `if ($right->dbID)` guard
  treated a failed `readFromDB()` as success; both handlers now test the read
  result (`>= tl::OK`) so invalid ids are dropped and an all-invalid payload
  yields the `E_EMPTYROLE` 400 (legacy `rolesEdit.php:102-103` parity)
  (Fixes #1535).
- Reflected XSS in the User Management tab bars: the four modern screens
  (`usersView.html`, `rolesView.html`, `usersAssignProject.html`,
  `usersAssignPlan.html`) concatenated the raw `tproject_id`/`tplan_id` URL
  params into the `href="..."` attribute of their tab anchors, so a crafted URL
  like `?tproject_id=1" onclick="alert(1)" x="` injected a `onclick` attribute
  into every tab (arbitrary JS in the logged-in session). Both params are now
  `encodeURIComponent()`-ed when the tab `ctx` query string is built (5 sites:
  usersView.html:254+317, rolesView.html:200, usersAssignProject.html:95,
  usersAssignPlan.html:87), making attribute breakout impossible; verified
  payload-free DOM on all 4 screens + full regression on tab nav, project/plan
  preselection (Fixes #1529).
