- `tree::getBottomOrder()` interpolated its `$parentID` argument raw into SQL
  (`WHERE parent_id={$parentID}`, tree.class.php:727) with no type/range check, so a
  non-numeric parent (a suite name like `WLK Suite`) produced a SQL error 1064 logged
  to `events` and a silently failing create/reorder — and was a SQL-injection class
  sink. `$parentID` is now int-cast at function entry (`intval()`), which drives any
  non-numeric input to the same safe default as an empty container (`max_order` 0)
  while leaving legitimate numeric ids byte-identical (Fixes #1526).
- Roles BFF `PUT /tproject-roles` / `PUT /tplan-roles` with an empty `assignments`
  map passed `array_keys([]) = []` into `deleteUserRoles()`, whose `!is_null($users)`
  branch built `AND user_id IN()` → MariaDB 1064, HTTP 500 and an `events` ERROR
  entry on a normal UI action. Both managers now treat an empty array as a no-op
  (return `tl::OK` without building SQL; `null` still deletes all roles of the
  feature) and the two BFF handlers short-circuit an empty/absent map to
  `{"status":"ok"}` like legacy `usersAssign.php:560-562` (Fixes #1523).
- `usersAssignProject.html` built the assignment map with `if (uid && roleVal > 0)`,
  filtering out every user whose role select was `-- no role --` (0). The BFF deletes
  only `array_keys($assignments)` before re-adding `rid > 0` (legacy
  `usersAssign.php:557-573`), so a user being un-assigned was silently skipped: map `{}`
  hit the empty-map no-op and `user_testproject_roles` kept the old role. The map
  builder now keeps `0` rows (`if (uid)`, identical to the already-correct
  `usersAssignPlan.html`), so clearing a role performs the DELETE exactly like legacy
  (Fixes #1524).
- `testcase::addAliens()` aborted with a PHP 8 `TypeError` on every tracker-less
  test project: `getInterfaceObject()` returns `null` when the project has no
  issue tracker linked, and line 10372 fed that `null` straight into
  `method_exists($repo,'addLink')` — PHP 8 requires an object|string first arg
  (PHP < 8 silently returned false), so the INSERT into `testcase_aliens`
  succeeded but the request fatally crashed. The tracker loop is now guarded
  with `!is_null($repo) &&`; the identical clone in `removeAlien()` (line 10481,
  `method_exists($repo,'removeLink')`) got the same guard (Fixes #1520).
