## 2.0.1 (in-progress)
### Key bugfix (i18n) — freeTestCases Importance badges no longer show the raw `high|medium|low` value in every locale; the badge text now maps through the existing `search.lowImportance|mediumImportance|highImportance` keys (Fixes #1874)
- `gui/templates/results/freeTestCases.html` `priorityBadge()` used the BFF's canonical token as the
  visible badge text, so Romanian/German/… users saw `high`/`low`/`medium` next to translated headers
  and filter options. The token now only selects the CSS class; the text goes through
  `t('search.<x>Importance', …)`. Client-side only — sort (`impRank`) and the `^low|medium|high$`
  LIST filter keep reading the raw datum, and no i18n bundle had to change (keys already existed in
  all 10 locales). Restores the legacy `lang_get()` hop (`lib/results/freeTestCases.php:53-62`).
  Regression suite `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md` (Issue #1874) 8/8 PASS, Event Viewer clean.

### Gap closed — Quick Search: the full legacy search-criteria form was dropped in `searchQuickView.html`, which exposed only the single quick-text box (Refs #1101)
- `gui/templates/search/searchQuickView.html` now has an expandable "Advanced criteria" panel
  (`#btnAdv` toggle + `#advPanel`) re-implementing EVERY legacy `tcSearch.php?doAction=userInput`
  criterion: Test Case ID (prefix ignored, hint shown), version, title, importance, status,
  created/edited by, summary, preconditions, steps, expected results, the four date ranges,
  Jolly (OR) (with a hint that it supersedes the text fields, legacy `tcSearch.php:93-121`
  semantics), keyword, custom field + value, requirement doc ID — plus the existing quick box
- The BFF `api/search/index.php` already parsed every filter, so the gap was purely front-end:
  new `buildAdvancedParams()`/`loadContext()` population/`resetForm()` clearing/`fmtDate()`,
  deep-link prefill (dates included) auto-opens the panel so filters are never invisible,
  all criteria combine with AND (verified against the BFF), quick text conflicts (advanced Title
  / Test Case ID set) surface a localized toast instead of silently dropping the input, Enter
  inside any advanced input triggers the search, an explicit advanced value wins over the quick box
- i18n: `search.advancedCriteria`, `search.quickIgnoredTc`, `search.quickIgnoredName`,
  `search.jollySupersedes` added and `search.prefixIgnored` reused in all 10 bundles;
  `ai/verify_i18n_coverage.sh` PASS (9 bundles, 0 failed)
- Mandatory code review (subagent) — no blockers; applied 7 findings (conflict toasts, caret
  state machine, label-in-name `aria-label` removal, jolly supersede hint, Enter handling, deep-link
  panel auto-open + date params, dead `title=""`); re-verified each in the browser
- Test suite: `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md` -> `Task — Issue #1101` re-run against `tmp/fixtures_1101.php`
  (QSDemo project, 5 TCs over 3 suites, keywords, custom field `qs_env`, requirement REQ-QS1):
  20+ criterion scenarios + date ranges + toast/warn paths + locale switch + Event Viewer clean
- Entry point: quick search launcher → `searchQuickView.html`; parity source
  `lib/testcases/tcSearch.php` + `lib/testcases/tcSearchForm.php`

### Key bugfix — `requirement_spec_mgr::get_by_id()` no longer interpolates an EMPTY revision id into SQL (Fixes #1714)
- `get_by_id()` resolved the latest revision via `get_last_child_info()` and read
  `$info['id']` unguarded: for a `req_specs` row with no revision (orphan) that
  raised an E_WARNING, then built `RSPEC_REV.id =   AND RSPEC.id = N` → SQL 1064,
  so `api/reqspec spec_view` answered HTTP 200 with the legacy HTML backtrace and
  wrote an ERROR pair to the Event Viewer. A single null/validity guard now
  returns `null` (the documented "query fails" contract) before any SQL is built,
  closing the same raw `RSPEC.id = {$id}` interpolation for all 39+5 call sites
  (Refs #1714). Regression suite `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md` (Issue #1714) 4/4 PASS,
  Event Viewer clean.

### Screen — Platform Create/Edit `platformsEdit` (Refs #1871)
- `gui/templates/platforms/platformsEdit.html` + `api/platformedit/index.php`: one Dashio page
  for both legacy modes of `lib/platforms/platformsEdit.php` (create + edit, now a session-guarded
  GET/HEAD-only 302 shim that forwards `tproject_id`/`platform_id`/`tplan_id`), with project/mode
  cards, name with the uniqueness hint, notes, the three legacy flags (enable on design /
  enable on execution / open for execution), Save/Cancel/Back/Refresh, delete-confirm modal and
  localized invalid-project / not-found / permission-denied state cards
- BFF rights: `platform_view` for init, `platform_management` for save/flag/delete, all re-checked
  on the OWNING test project; foreign (project, platform) pairs answer 404 before any name probe;
  duplicate names answer 422 `E_NAMEALREADYEXISTS` on BOTH create and update; a platform linked
  to a test plan answers 422 `DELETE_BLOCKED`; wrong verbs 405 + `Allow`, POST without the
  same-origin proof 403 (CSRF), anon 401, no-rights 403 + `audit_security_user_right_missing`
- Four defects found while testing, each fixed in its own commit: `fdff038ba` (duplicate name on
  create returned the raw legacy `-4` code the screen cannot localize), `6fea33193` (the legacy
  shim answered 302 to a POST), `91d11416c` (the MODE card stayed "Create" after a successful
  create flipped the screen into edit mode), `b03ded011` (Dashio Bootstrap JS was never included,
  so `$(...).modal is not a function` left the delete-confirm modal dead)
- Entry points: `platformsView.html` Edit/Create buttons, `$actions->platformEdit` in
  `lib/functions/common.php`; `pedit.*` + `footers.platformsEdit` keys present in all bundles
  (i18n key-set gate PASS, shared `pedit.*` namespace with the Test Project editor has no key
  collisions — verified by set intersection)
- Test suite: `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md` -> `TC-1871` re-run in full against the fresh fixture
  `tmp/fixtures_1871.php` (project PLED1871/foreign PLFOR/plan/platforms/user `plednorights`):
  16 API checks + 19 browser checks + shim/wiring, all PASS; suite gate `TLU_REQUIRE_SUITE=1871`
  7/7. Event Viewer clean (the single WARNING row came from the throwaway fixture itself)
- Mandatory **code review** (subagent) then applied 3 findings: session gate
  moved BEFORE the DB connect (#1677/#1780/#1814 - a DB failure can no longer answer an
  anonymous caller with a raw `dbms_msg`), `init` now checks rights BEFORE resolving the
  test project (uniform 403 for unknown and foreign projects - the #1697 existence-oracle
  lesson, measured byte-identical 403 for id 99999 vs 13 with the role-3 user), and a
  server-side 100-char name cap (varchar(100) / legacy PLATFORM_MAXLEN) -> 422
  E_NAMELENGTH; the review's other claims (CSRF, SQLi, XSS in toasts, out() status reset,
  verb contract) were disproven by the executed verification matrix.
- Docs/wiki `Modernize-Platforms-Edit-platformsEdit.md` + 9 screenshots
  `docs/screenshots/issue-1871-platformsedit-*.png` (Refs #1871)

### Screen — Custom Field Editor `cfieldsEdit` (Refs #1812)
- `gui/templates/cfields/cfieldsEdit.html` + `api/cfieldsedit/index.php`: one Dashio
  page for both legacy modes of `lib/cfields/cfieldsEdit.php` (create + edit + delete),
  covering every function the modernized list/assign screens had only partially ported:
  the standalone editor with Name/Label/Type/Available-on/Enable-on/show-on combos,
  Possible-Values field, name-uniqueness probe, the `is_used()` lock (used fields get a
  read-only Type + Available-on with a lock badge and a warning banner), enable-on →
  show-on-execution propagation, "Add and assign", and a delete-confirm modal; legacy
  `lib/cfields/cfieldsEdit.php` survives as a session-guarded GET-302 / write-405 shim.
  BFF contract: session + `bffSameOriginGuard` on writes, `cfield_management` on the
  ADDRESSED test project, `{status,code,message}` JSON, POST-only mutations; measured
  401 anon / 403 `no_right` (role-3 user) / 404 unknown cfield / 405 bad verb+action /
  409 `name_exists` / 400 `type_locked` (used field) / 400
  `area_not_allowed_for_node_type` (req-spec node on execution). A bare `do_action=create`
  starts a clean form even when `cfield_id` is present (legacy `$query['do_action']`
  semantics — enter/edit mode needs `do_action=edit&cfield_id=N`).
- Entry points: `cfieldsView.html` Edit/Create buttons + `$actions->cfieldsEdit` in
  `lib/functions/common.php`; `cfed.*` + `footers.cfieldsEdit` keys across all 10 bundles
  (i18n key-set gate PASS: 6959 keys, 0 missing per bundle).
- Test suite: `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md` -> Issue #1812 34/34 PASS (API contract matrix,
  shim branches, browser cases incl. used-field lock + `ro` locale switch of the dynamic
  form, wiring/lint, Event Viewer clean — only AUDIT `log_level=16` rows, the serialized
  `tlMetaStringHelper` in `events.description` is the standard logger format on read).
- Screenshots `docs/screenshots/issue-1812-cfieldsedit-01-create.png` /
  `-02-edit-used-locked.png` / `-03-delete-confirm.png` + docs/wiki
  `Modernize-Custom-Field-Editor-cfieldsEdit.md` (Refs #1812)

### Screen — Configuration Check / Security Notes `configCheck` (Refs #1814)
- The security notes that legacy computed on every page load
  (`lib/functions/configCheck.php getSecurityNotes()`) were no longer rendered
  by any 2.0.1 screen; and in `FILE`/`SILENT` warning modes the legacy helper
  dropped them after writing them to `log_path/config_check.txt`
- New read-only BFF `api/configcheck/index.php` (`GET ?action=init`) reuses the
  SAME legacy helpers in the exact legacy check order (install dir → auth/LDAP
  → admin default pwd → BTS connection → repository dir → schema → email →
  extensions), returns every note as `{code,text}` regardless of mode, plus
  `mode`, destination `file`, `count`, `appVersion` and a `legacy_function`
  traceability field; session-gated BEFORE the DB connect (401), verb-guarded
  (405 + Allow), scalar action guard (400), client `locale` maps onto
  `lang_get` like `api/cfields`
- New Dashio screen `gui/templates/conf/configCheck.html` (mode/file/count/
  version meta strip, per-note code chips, "all checks passed" empty state,
  401/403/404/400/405/500 state cards, Refresh/Back/Close, locale switcher)
- The Home dashboard (`mainPage.html`) gained an amber advisory banner shown
  only when the BFF reports warnings, linking to the screen in a new tab
- `$actions->configCheck` deep link in `lib/functions/common.php`; 23 i18n
  keys (`ccn.*` + `footers.configCheck`) in all 10 bundles
- Docs/wiki `Config-Check-Security-Notes-1814.md` + screenshots (Refs #1814)

### Screen — Test Suite Create / Edit / Delete `suiteEdit` (Refs #1852)
- `gui/templates/testcases/suiteEdit.html` + `api/suiteedit`: one Dashio page for
  the three legacy modes of `lib/testcases/containerEdit.php` (`new_testsuite` /
  `add_testsuite` / `edit_testsuite` / `update_testsuite` / `delete_testsuite`,
  now 302-redirected to it), restoring the test-suite **design custom fields**
  (`design_values_to_db()`), the keyword assignment and the legacy
  `delete_executed_testcases` gate that the inline `api/suiteview` modal had
  silently dropped
- Every custom-field type is rendered from data only (label, type name and
  possible values arrive from the API, never from `innerHTML`)
- Delete mode shows the blast radius (nested suites + deep test cases), the
  per-case path and link/execution status table, blocks the action with 409
  `suite_has_executed` when an executed case is found, and only navigates away
  after the server confirms the write
- Entry points switched: `suiteView.html` (New Sub-Suite / Edit Suite / Delete
  Suite), `testSpec.html` (New Test Suite), `common.php` (`$actions->suiteEdit`
  / `suiteCreate` / `suiteDelete`); 58 i18n keys in all ten bundles
- Bugs filed while testing: #1853 (`_build_cfield()` treats any
  `custom_field_*_input` key as a DATE part → `tlStringLen(array)` fatal) and
  #1854 (`check_string()` answers "forbidden characters" for a string that does
  not match the pattern)
- The mandatory **browser pass** (real clicks, real reloads, real DB reads) then
  fixed 6 defects the API matrix cannot see: the CF block died on a
  multiselection field (a `var` read out of the checkbox branch, taking the
  keyword picker with it); **every save wiped the suite's keywords** (the Assigned
  options were never `selected`, and only `:selected` options are sent); the form
  was saveable exactly once per page load (`BUSY` was never released on the
  success path, so later clicks vanished silently); 33 `E_WARNING` per page load
  from a DATE-only custom field (`$m[4..6]` of the optional time group); the
  legacy redirect dropped the suite/container identity when it was reached with
  `suite_id`/`container_id`; and keyword writes were unvalidated, so foreign
  keyword ids could be attached (`400 keyword_mismatch` now)
- Test suite: `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md` -> `## Issue #1852`, 51 PASS / 1 SKIPPED /
  0 FAIL, of which 15 cases are the browser pass
### Gap closed — Search Test Cases: the result grid lost the legacy group-by-Test-Suite ExtTable behaviour (Fixes #1092)
- `gui/templates/search/searchView.html` rendered the quick-search hits as a FLAT
  DataTable, dropping everything `lib/testcases/tcSearch.php:339-351`
  (`buildExtTable`) configured: `setGroupByColumnName('test_suite')` +
  `setSortByColumnName('test_case')` + `sortDirection='DESC'` +
  `showToolbar=true` + `allowMultiSort=false`.
  The rows are now grouped per test-suite path under a collapsible teal header
  `Suite Alpha (3 Items)` (legacy `groupTextTpl '{text} (N Items)'`,
  `lib/functions/exttable.class.php:591`) with the new
  `rowGroup.dataTables` plugin, the grid toolbar returns with the
  `Expand/Collapse Groups` button (the only button legacy showed for this screen:
  `toolbarRefreshButton`/`toolbarShowAllColumnsButton` are false in
  `tcSearch.php:349-350` and `storeTableState=false` suppresses the default-state
  button, `inc_ext_table.tpl:187-206`), plus a `Show all Columns` /
  `Hide Test Suite column` toggle for the legacy `hideGroupedColumn=true` state
  (`exttable.class.php:55`) that legacy could never undo. Default order is
  suite path asc (RowGroup merges only contiguous runs, so the grouped column must
  stay the primary sort criterion) then test case **desc**, `orderMulti:false`
  mirrors `allowMultiSort=false`, and the no-CDN fallback `<tbody>` (#799) carries
  the same group headers. Result rows became objects so ordering uses the raw
  path while the visible cell stays escaped. No BFF change: `api/search/index.php`
  already returns `path` per row. 7 new i18n keys (`sv.grid.*`) in **all 10**
  bundles.
### KEY BUGFIX — a failed code-tracker database connection produced NO Event Viewer record: `codeTrackerInterface::connect()` built `$connection_args` with two-level simple string interpolation, so PHP interpolated the `stdClass` `$this->cfg` (from `setCfg():147 json_decode(json_encode(...))`) and raised a fatal `Error` one line *before* the `tLog()` (Fixes #1703)
- `lib/codetrackerintegration/codeTrackerInterface.class.php:188-189` — wrapped the three
  property reads in `{}` (`"Host:{$this->cfg->dbhost} - "`), identical to the issue-tracker twin
  already fixed in #1701 (`issueTrackerInterface.class.php:241`). PHP resolves only ONE property
  level in a non-curly interpolated string, so the old line emitted the literal fragments
  `Host:->dbhost - DBName: ->dbname - User: ->dbuser` — and because `setCfg():147` makes `cfg` a
  `stdClass`, stringifying it aborted the statement outright. Post-fix the diagnostic records
  `Host:127.0.0.1 - DBName: nodb - User: nodb` together with the ADODB message.
  Blast radius: **2 lines, 1 file** — a repo-wide sweep for unbraced `"$this->X->Y"` found no
  other unfixed site. Latent, not currently firing: `tlCodeTracker::$systems` registers only
  `stash` and `github` and both override `connect()`, so no UI route reaches the base method —
  it is an armed fatal for the next `db`-API tracker / subclass inheriting `connect()`.
  Regression matrix R1-R8 + guards I1-I4 recorded in `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md`.
### KEY BUGFIX (i18n) — `gui/templates/i18n/fr.json` missed 26 keys `en.json` defines, so `fr_FR` users saw raw dotted keys (`role.noRights`) on screen (Fixes #1840)
- `TLi18n.t()` resolves as `_strings[key] || key` (`gui/templates/i18n/i18n.js:165`), so a key missing from the loaded bundle has **no fallback layer**: the module returned the key itself and `apply()` wrote it into `textContent`, overwriting the English literal in the HTML. Added the 26 keys (`rctc.*` 6, `role.*` 6, `ts.*` 4, `rmo.grid.*` 7, `rmo.*` 3) with French translations at their alphabetical position; `{count}` preserved. Key-set diff `fr` vs `en`: 26 -> 0. The ASIDE `Test Strategy`/`Documentation` symptom in the report is a **different** i18n layer (legacy `locale/fr_FR/strings.txt`, filed as #1843); the `de`/`es`/`it` twins and a coverage CI gate were filed as #1844.
