### Key bugfix — Req. Management System interface instantiation: legacy Requirements screens died with an empty HTTP 500 (Fixes #1629)
- Key bugfix #1629: `tlReqMgrSystem::getInterfaceObject()` (`lib/functions/tlReqMgrSystem.class.php:646`)
  was the **third and last** unguarded `new` in the class, after `checkConnection()` and the
  `getAll()` `checkEnv` guard that #1625 hardened. `lib/functions/common.php:140` already
  named it as the outstanding one. Reproduced (the report was filed unverified, because the
  freshly imported CI database has no project linked to a ReqMgr system — the fixture is
  created by `tmp/verify_1629.sh`): with `testprojects.reqmgr_integration_enabled=1` and a
  `testproject_reqmgrsystem` link, **every** legacy Requirements screen answered
  **HTTP 500 with a 0-byte body** — `reqSpecEdit.php:23`, `reqSpecSearch.php:34` and
  `reqSpecViewRevision.php:59` all build a `reqSpecCommands`, whose constructor calls the
  method at `reqSpecCommands.class.php:44`. Because that call sits in a **constructor**, the
  fatal fires before a single byte is flushed, so the user gets a blank page, and because the
  process dies before `shutdownLogger()` the Event Viewer stays **empty** — a silent 500.
  Two flavours, both measured on line 657: `type=1` resolves to `contoursoapInterface`
  (`getImplementationForType()`, `:111`), a class not shipped here and never was
  (`git log --all -- '*contour*'` is empty) → `Error: Class "contoursoapInterface" not found`;
  and a `type` that is not a key of `$systems` makes `getByAttr()` (`:344`) store
  `implementation = NULL` → `Error: Class name must be a valid object or a string`. The
  `catch (Exception $e)` in the same method **never applied** — an `Error` is not an
  `Exception`.

  Fix: return `null` when `getByID()` found nothing or `implementation` is missing / not a
  string / not loadable (`!@class_exists($iname)` — the `@` is required, otherwise the
  autoloader's `include_once()` writes the two #1593 E_WARNING rows per request), and widen
  the handler to `catch (Throwable)` so a throwable from a *shipped* implementation class
  degrades too. Returning `null` is provably safe for the only caller:
  `reqSpecCommands.class.php:44` **discards** the return value (`$rms` is never read; line 45
  overwrites it with `getLinkedTo()`), and `null` is what this method already returns when no
  system is linked, and what `tlIssueTracker::getInterfaceObject()` returns for the same case.
  No i18n change (no user-facing string added or removed), no template change, no BFF change.
  Verified on the *render* path `reqSpecEdit.php?doAction=create` (NOT `doAction=init`:
  `init` is not a `renderGui()` case label, so it answers with the 28-byte
  `Can not process RENDERING!!!` stub even when the screen is healthy — measured
  pre/post **`500` / 0 bytes → `200` / 15645 bytes**); 0 new `events` rows; the dangling-link
  and integration-off paths unchanged; a *loadable* implementation class is still really
  instantiated (a shipped stub class proves the guard is not over-broad) and a `TypeError`
  raised by such a class's constructor on a `NULL` `cfg` (the column is nullable, so that is
  normal data) is caught by the widened handler; the #1625 siblings
  (`reqMgrSystemView.php`, `reqMgrSystemEdit.php?doAction=checkConnection`) and the
  modernized `api/reqmgrsystems` / `api/reqspec` BFFs unchanged. Regression suite 1629
  37/37 PASS (`bash tmp/verify_1629.sh`, exit 0; pre-fix baseline 10 FAIL / exit 1, so the
  harness is discriminating). Masked-but-separate defects found while testing and filed, not
  fixed: **#1735** (`reqSpecSearch.php:116` `count(null)` — the #1629 fatal used to kill the
  request before that line, and the fix uncovers it) and **#1736** (`renderGui()` at
  `reqSpecEdit.php:147` reading a `null` `$opObj` for an unrecognised `doAction`).
  (Fixes #1629)

