### KEY BUGFIX — `tlReqMgrSystem::delete()` leaked an internal class/method prefix into the delete message (Fixes #1728)
### KEY BUGFIX — every create of a requirement management system wrote an E_WARNING Event Viewer row (Fixes #1729)
### KEY BUGFIX — the editor BFF: array-shaped parameters logged warnings and could be stored as the name `Array` (Fixes #1730)
### KEY BUGFIX (security) — stored DOM XSS: an unescaped system name was injected into the editor's feedback banner (Fixes #1731)
### KEY BUGFIX — the `reqMgrSystemEdit.php` 302 shim: array-shaped `$_REQUEST` wrote an E_WARNING *and* an ERROR row into the Event Viewer on every request (Fixes #1731)
- `is_scalar()` guards (`shimReqScalar`/`shimReqInt`, the same idiom as `lib/attachments/attachmentdelete.php`
  and `api/reqmgrsystemedit/index.php`). `?doAction[]=x` raised `E_WARNING Array to string conversion`
  (2 rows/request, 5 requests = 10) and the coerced `"Array"` then tripped the `default:` branch's
  `tLog(...,'ERROR')`; `?tproject_id[]=1` was silently `intval()`'d to 1 — the wrong test project, with
  no diagnostic at all. Reachable from ANY authenticated session: the shim has no rights check. Array
  `doAction` is refused early at INFO (never ERROR) with a 302 to the list screen — this file is a
  bookmark redirector, so a junk query string must not become a 400. Docs
  `docs/Bugfix-Issue-1731-ReqMgrSystemEdit-Shim-Array-Request-E_WARNING.md`.

### KEY BUGFIX — the legacy `reqSpecEdit.php`: an unrenderable `doAction` wrote 3 E_WARNING rows + answered a 28-byte blank page, and its internal helpers answered a SILENT HTTP 500 (Fixes #1736)
- `lib/requirements/reqSpecEdit.php:37` dispatched with `method_exists($commandMgr,$pFn)`. That is not a
  whitelist of requestable GUI actions: it also matches the INTERNAL HELPERS of `reqSpecCommands`
  (24 `method_exists`-visible members, only **18** of them GUI actions), and the dispatch invoked
  whatever it matched with a fixed 2-argument signature `$pFn($args,$_REQUEST)`. One unknown
  `doAction` therefore had FIVE different outcomes, measured:
  | `doAction` | before | after |
  |---|---|---|
  | unknown / absent / empty / `bogus` / `CREATE` | HTTP 200, **28 bytes** (`Can not process RENDERING!!!`) + **3** `E_WARNING` rows at `reqSpecEdit.php:147` | HTTP **302** -> `reqSpecMgmt.html`, **0** rows |
  | `simpleCompare` (reqParams=4), `process_revision` (3) | **HTTP 500, 0 bytes, 0 log rows** | HTTP 302, 0 rows |
  | `initGuiObjForAttachmentOperations` (**private**) | **HTTP 500, 0 bytes, 0 log rows** | HTTP 302, 0 rows |
  | `initGuiBean` / `getReqMgrSystem` (reqParams=0) | **HTTP 500, 0 bytes** | HTTP 302, 0 rows |
  | `?doAction[]=x` | **HTTP 500, 0 bytes** — `trim(array)` `TypeError` in `inputparameter.class.php:295`, before this controller ran at all | HTTP 302, 0 rows |
  The 500 half is the worse half: a 0-byte body with **zero** Event Viewer rows leaves an operator
  nothing to grep. The two claims in the issue body that `initialize_gui()` can return `null` and
  that the object at fault is `$gui` are both wrong and are corrected in the issue trail.
- Fix, all inside `lib/requirements/reqSpecEdit.php` (+161/-2): **(C1)** `reqSpecEditActionWhitelist()` —
  a whitelist that is the EXACT 18-case list of `renderGui()`'s GUI-rendering switch, consulted with
  `is_string($pFn) && $pFn !== '' && isset($list[$pFn])`, so arity and visibility match by construction;
  **(C2)** `reqSpecEditRefuseUnknownAction()` — one `tLog(...,'INFO')` row with a **fixed literal**
  message (the requested value is attacker controlled and is deliberately NOT interpolated) and a 302 back
  to `gui/templates/requirements/reqSpecMgmt.html` with `tproject_id` carried forward. INFO does not
  persist below WARNING, so a crafted query string can not write an Error/Warning row: measured 0 rows
  of ANY level for a request that used to write 3. Same remedy #1627/#1722 established in
  `lib/reqmgrsystems/reqMgrSystemEdit.php:87-103`; **(C3)** `reqSpecEditDropShapedAction()` drops a
  non-scalar `$_REQUEST['doAction']` before `R_PARAMS()` (the same local-shim idiom as #1731, rather than
  changing the shared input layer — filed separately), plus a null-guard on `renderGui()`'s `default:`
  branch as defence in depth.
- **The shared cause was deliberately NOT changed**: `lib/functions/inputparameter.class.php:295`
  calls `trim()` unconditionally, so an array-shaped value for ANY `STRING_N` parameter of ANY
  controller is an uncaught `TypeError` (500 / 0 bytes / 0 rows) — filed as **#1738** so the blast
  radius is fixed once at the root instead of N times per screen.
- Verified error-free: 32-case regression suite (cases 1-17 the refused actions, 18-23d every
  whitelisted action, 24 a real `doCreate` POST writing 1 new `req_specs` row, 25 an 18/18 pre-fix vs
  post-fix equivalence sweep, 28 three hostile `doAction` values producing 0 rows of any level,
  30-31 the whitelist<->switch invariant and "no in-repo caller is broken"); `php -l`; browser check
  that `?doAction=init` lands on `RSE1736 - Requirement Specification Management` while
  `?doAction=create` still renders the full editor; **0** new Error/Warning rows from the fix.
  Three bugs found while testing and filed, NOT fixed here (each measured identical on the pre-fix
  code): **#1737** `reqSpecCommands.class.php:844` (`deleteFile()` never sets `$argsObj->uploadOp`) and
  `:877` (`bulkReqMon()` `foreach(null)` on an empty spec) each write an E_WARNING row per request;
  **#1739** `lib/requirements/reqEdit.php:41` and `lib/plan/planMilestonesEdit.php:30` still carry the
  same `method_exists()` dispatch shape. Docs: `docs/Bugfix-Issue-1736-ReqSpecEdit-Unrenderable-Action.md`.
  (Fixes #1736)

### Screen — Duplicate Name Check `nameCheck` (Refs #1724)
- Modernizes the GENERIC node name-uniqueness backend `lib/ajax/checkNodeDuplicateName.php`, which
  admitted in its own header that it performed "no check on user rights" and had no project scope:
  any authenticated session could POST a `parent_id` from ANY test project and learn whether a node
  name was taken. Its sibling `lib/ajax/checkDuplicateName.php` gated on the GLOBAL `mgt_view_tc`,
  letting a holder of that right enumerate test case names in every other project. Both endpoints
  are now session-guarded, resolve the OWNING project of the addressed parent and check
  `mgt_view_tc` OR `mgt_modify_tc` there.
- `gui/templates/testcases/nameCheck.html` (Dashio, context + name-to-check + result cards, live
  debounced check, collision table, AVAILABLE/DUPLICATE/ERROR chip, TLi18n) + BFF
  `api/namecheck/index.php` (`init` / `check`, same-origin guard, session window, parent-scoped
  collisions as in `tree::nodeNameExists()`, self-exclusion only for a genuine sibling, full
  400/401/403/404/405 contract). Reachable from a new ASIDE item in the Test Specification section.
  The check stays a WARNING, never a save gate — exact 1.9.20 behaviour.

### KEY BUGFIX — a test SUITE name check always failed with `parent_not_found` (Fixes #1725)
- The owning-project walk read `parent_id` before the node's own `node_type_id`. A test suite is a
  direct child of the test project root, whose own `parent_id` is 0, so the walk bailed out before
  classifying the root: the screen's headline use case answered 404 while the deeper test-case
  variant worked and hid the defect. The node's own type is now tested first (BFF + both shims).
- Also fixed by the mandatory code review: a deep link with a foreign `parent_id` was a silent
  `<select>` no-op that rendered a green "Available" for a real duplicate; changing the node type
  left the previous verdict on screen; a test case addressed at project level answered "Available";
  no-rights callers could enumerate project/node ids via 403-vs-404; `?action[]=x` emitted a PHP 8
  `Array to string conversion` warning; and a foreign `node_id` could suppress a real collision.

