  this entry the modernization ledger has **0 TODO screens** (every ASIDE entry maps to a modern
  `.html` + BFF).
- New screen `gui/templates/testcases/containerMoveTC.html` (Dashio: teal header + dark toolbar with
  the project / source-suite context and the TLi18n locale switcher, a Destination card with the
  dotted `gen_combo_test_suites()` list where the **source suite is a disabled option**, the
  Copy Keywords / Copy Requirement Assignments pair plus the hint that a Move ignores both, a Test
  Cases card with Select all / Clear selection, a live counter and one row per case carrying
  `#PREFIX-N`, name, summary and the Status / Importance / Execution labels produced by
  `getConfigAndLabels()` (the same source the legacy screen read at `containerEdit.php:1030-1040`),
  Move / Copy / Copy as Ghost Steps behind a Bootstrap confirm modal, and loading / green result /
  red error / red access-denied / empty-suite states).
- BFF `api/tcmovecopy/index.php` (`GET ?action=init&tproject_id=&suite_id=`,
  `POST ?action=move|copy|copy_ghost`): session auth + `bffEnforceSession` + `bffSameOriginGuard`,
  `mgt_modify_tc` on the **owning** project, the source suite proven to be a `testsuite` node of it,
  the destination proven to be a `testsuite` of the **same** project, **every submitted id proven to
  be a test case of the source suite**, destination != source, writes POST-only, 400/401/403/404/
  405/409 with stable machine codes the screen maps to its own i18n key. `$actions->containerMoveTC`
  registered in `lib/functions/common.php`; the four legacy actions are intercepted in
  `lib/testcases/containerEdit.php` right after `$args->action = $action;` (the interception cannot
  live inside `init_args()`: it needs the ids that function resolves, while `$action` is only known
  after the submit-button loop) and 302-redirect to the modern screen carrying the old selection
  (`objectIDs[]` or `objectID`), the destination (`containerID`) and the intent (`pending_action`)
  behind an explicit "nothing has been changed yet" notice. Every other action of that controller is
  untouched.
- Legacy parity kept: the three write intents, the disabled source suite, both copy flags, the
  dotted suite list, the per-case label columns and the empty-suite message. Hardened beyond it -
  see the security note below.
- i18n `tmvc.*` (50) + `footers.containerMoveTC` in all 10 bundles, **appended** (a first
  `sort_keys=True` attempt rewrote ~2400 unrelated lines and was reverted - the bundles are shared
  with the concurrent CI agents).
- 3 defects found by the mandatory browser pass, all fixed in `1ffd36bf6`: the repo vendors
  **Bootstrap 3.4.1**, not 5, so the BS5 `new bootstrap.Modal()` threw `ReferenceError: bootstrap is
  not defined` and the confirm dialog never opened; the success banner was rendered *before* the
  post-write reload and `load()` clears the boxes, so every successful move/copy was silently
  swallowed; and `http_build_query()` encodes the selection as `tcase_ids[0]`, so the
  `'[?&]tcase_ids[]='` regex never matched and a legacy deep link lost its whole selection (now
  `URLSearchParams`).
- 7 class-API traps documented in the docs page for the next screen, each of which produced a
  blank-bodied 500 first: there is **no** `getDBTables()` global (use `tlObjectWithDB::getDBTables()`);
  `config_get('testproject_options')` returns the config **key name as a string** (use
  `testproject::getOptions()`); `testcase::get_by_id($id, $version_id, $filters, $options)` takes **no
  `$db`**; its rows use `id` (the tcversion id), `importance` (**not** `priority`), `testsuite_id`
  (**not** `parent_id`), `is_open` (**not** `open`) - a wrong key returns empty/0 **silently**;
  `fetchFirstRowSingleColumn()` needs its column argument; there is **no** `tlLog()` function; and
  there is no locale key for "N test cases moved", so - matching `api/tcbulkop`, the comparable
  modern screen - the write paths add no `events` audit row (that would need new `$TLS_...` keys in
  all 19 server locales).
- Verified by 44 numbered cases in `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md` (Suite 1724), 44/44 PASS, plus the browser
  matrix (move / copy / ghost / empty / denied / error / RO locale / legacy deep link), console
  clean and the Event Viewer clean (0 new Error/Warning rows; the only `log_level=2` rows name
  `Command line code`, i.e. this run's own DB probes). Docs
  `docs/Modernize-Move-Copy-Test-Cases-containerMoveTC.md` + wiki page + 8 screenshots.

### KEY BUGFIX (security) — the three legacy move/copy actions were cross-site-postable GET forms that never checked rights nor ownership (Refs #1724)
- `lib/testcases/containerEdit.php` submitted `do_move_tcase_set` / `do_copy_tcase_set` /
  `do_copy_tcase_set_ghost` as plain forms that read `$_REQUEST` (so a GET mutated), called no
  `hasRight()` for them and never proved the submitted `objectID` / `objectIDs[]` belonged to the
  suite on screen. Any authenticated session could therefore relink a test case of **any** test
  project into an arbitrary suite, and any third-party page could make a logged-in user post it.
  They are now session-guarded 302 shims onto the BFF, which enforces `mgt_modify_tc` on the owning
  project, proves every id and requires POST + same-origin.

### Gap closed — Requirement Spec Management: the legacy requirements filter panel was missing entirely (Fixes #1025)
- 1.9.20's Requirement Specification Management screen shipped `inc_filter_panel.tpl`, driven by
  `tlRequirementFilterControl` (lib/functions/tlRequirementFilterControl.class.php), and the server
  applied it through `get_filtered_req_map()` (lib/functions/treeMenu.inc.php:1753-1889). The 2.0.1
  rewrite of `reqSpecMgmt.html` dropped the whole panel: no Document ID, Title, Status, Requirement
  Type, Spec Type, Expected Coverage, Relation, Test Case ID or Custom Field filtering, and no
  Apply/Reset/Simple-Advanced/auto-refresh. On a project with more than a handful of specs there
  was no way to narrow the list at all.
- The filter is now ported end to end. BFF (`api/reqspec/index.php`): `readReqFilters()` normalises
  the request with the LEGACY rules (an `Any` = `0` entry anywhere in a multi-select disables that
  whole filter; a Test Case ID equal to the bare project prefix is disabled; every string goes
  through `$db->prepare_string()`), `reqFilterSql()` reproduces the legacy JOIN set and WHERE
  clause - including the `req_coverage` join for a Test Case ID and the `req_relations` join for a
  relation filter - and `reqFilteredMap()` feeds it to BOTH `action=specs` and `action=reqs`, so a
  specification whose own plus subtree requirements no longer match is pruned from the list, exactly
  as legacy did. `action=options` publishes the filter domains (`reqStatuses`, `reqTypes`,
  `specTypes`, `relationTypes`, `filterCFields`, `tcPrefix`, `childRequirementsManagement`).
  A single `reqFilteredMap()` call now resolves the whole spec subtree, replacing a per-spec query.
- Front end (`gui/templates/requirements/reqSpecMgmt.html`): Dashio filter panel with all 9 legacy
  controls, the project Custom Field inputs, matching-count badges, Apply / Reset Filters, and
  Simple <-> Advanced (Advanced turns the single selects into multi-selects, Simple warns before
  trimming a multi-selection). The "Update list after every operation" setting is honoured, and
  **Apply is authoritative** - typing alone does not re-query, which is what the legacy button
  driven panel did.
- Two review findings applied: an "equal" relation is now published under its BARE relation id
  (`3`, "related to") instead of a key the select could not emit, so it resolves to "either side of
  `req_relations`"; and switching Advanced -> Simple with a multi-selection warns instead of
  silently discarding the extra choices.
- Deliberate deviation, documented in the code: filtering is evaluated on the LATEST spec revision
  / requirement version. Legacy matched any revision, which on the modern tables (built from the
  latest revision) could return rows the table never shows.
- i18n: 20 new `rsf.*` keys in ALL 10 locale bundles (`de,en,es,fr,it,ja,pt,ro,ru,zh`).
- Verified: regression suite 1025 = **40/40 PASS** (2 syntax/JSON gates, 401 + 22 BFF filter cases
  across both actions, the legacy `Any`/prefix-only/equal-relation/subtree-pruning rules, an SQLi
  probe returning 0 rows with no error, 7 live browser interactions incl. Advanced, the Custom Field
  toggle and requirement-level filtering, a clean console, and Event Viewer with 0 new
  Error/Warning rows). (Fixes #1025)
