### Gap closed — Assign Test Plan Roles: the role select never pre-selected the EFFECTIVE plan role (Fixes #1664)
- `gui/templates/usermanagement/usersAssignPlan.html` seeded the per-user role
  `<select>` with the user's **explicit** `user_testplan_roles` row
  (`roleVal: u.roleID`, `0` when there is none), so every user without an
  explicit plan role opened on the value-0 "*revert to inherited …*" option.
  Legacy `usersAssign.tpl:249-256` pre-selects the **effective** plan role
  (`$applySelected`), which `get_tplan_effective_role()` resolves to
  `TL_ROLES_NO_RIGHTS` (3) with `is_inherited=0` for every non-admin user on a
  **private** test plan (`lib/functions/roles.inc.php:407-416`) — i.e. legacy
  opened the dropdown on `<no rights>`. Because the value-0 option was
  pre-selected, a plain Save submitted `userRole[<uid>]=0` and `doUpdate()`
  **deleted** those rows instead of materialising the explicit `<no rights>`
  plan role legacy writes. The BFF already shipped the right value
  (`effectiveRoleID` + `isInherited`, #944) but nothing consumed it for the
  select. Fix: `loadUsers()` now seeds `roleVal: u.isInherited ? 0 :
  u.effectiveRoleID` while `origRoleID` keeps the explicit row as the baseline —
  the same rule as the sibling screen (`usersAssignProject.html:390`).
- Because the legacy preselect makes `roleVal !== origRoleID` true for every
  `<no rights>` row **without any user edit**, the "Modified" bookkeeping can no
  longer derive from that comparison (it would enable Save on load). Rows now
  carry an explicit `changed` flag (sibling screen's `changedMap` pattern) set by
  `onRoleChange()` / `applyBulkRole()` against `origRoleID`, and consumed by
  `isDirty()`, the DataTables `createdRow` highlight and the badge. The Save
  payload (`assignments[u.id] = u.roleVal`) is unchanged — legacy always posts
  every non-admin row — so a plain Save now writes the explicit `<no rights>`
  rows like legacy `doUpdate()`. No BFF change, no new i18n key (the `<no
  rights>` label comes from the localized role list). Suite 1664 10/10 PASS,
  Event Viewer clean. Unrelated pre-existing `assignDt.cell()` TypeError found
  while testing filed as #1680. (Fixes #1664)
### Key bugfix — Reorder Test Steps: dead handlers after picker navigation, `no_change` on every write, literal `{count}` (Fixes #1674)
- `gui/templates/testcases/tcStepReorder.html` bound all 8 delegated handlers
  (picker row, move buttons, modal backdrop, 5 drag events, Discard) inside an
  `if/else` on `TCVER_ID`. The screen toggles its two cards in place, so whichever
  branch did not run at first paint was **permanently dead**: entering via the
  version picker rendered the step table with every write button, the
  drag-and-drop and "Discard changes" inert (0 POSTs left the browser, no
  console error), and entering via `?tcversion_id=N` left the "Change version"
  picker rows inert. Handlers are now bound unconditionally, branching only the
  initial load (lines 671-741).
- `api/tcstepsreorder/index.php` `tsroWriteResult()` compared the **sorted** id
  sequences before and after a write. The id set is invariant under every
  operation the screen performs (only `step_number` changes), so **every**
  successful write answered `status=no_change`: the move persisted but the user
  saw no success notice. It now compares the ordered id sequence **and** the
  ordered `step_number` sequence (`tsroNumbersOf()`), which also makes
  `?action=normalize` correctly report a real repair (`11,12,13,14 → 1,2,3,4`)
  instead of a no-op. Genuine no-ops (idempotent renumber, boundary move,
  reorder to the stored order) still answer `no_change` (line 463-468).
- `tcsr.normalizeConfirm` / `tcsr.renumbered` were rendered verbatim, so the
  renumber dialog read *"Renumber the steps from 1 to {count} …"*. Both call
  sites now pass `{ count: STEPS.length }` to `TLi18n.t()` (lines 636, 651).
- Regression suite `Regression — Issue #1674` in `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md`:
  **11/11 PASS**, Event Viewer clean (1 row, the login notice).

### Key bugfix — BFF CSRF guard accepted a FOREIGN `Origin` whenever `X-Requested-With` was present (Fixes #1679)
- `api/_guard.php` `bffSameOriginGuard()` returned success the moment it saw
  `X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest`, **before** reading `Origin`/`Referer`, so the
  authoritative same-origin signal was dead code whenever that header was present and a
  cross-origin `POST`/`PUT`/`DELETE`/`PATCH` was accepted as same-origin.
- The guard is the **only** CSRF control in the BFF layer — **101** endpoint files / **107**
  call sites invoke it, **102** files `include` `api/_guard.php` (101 endpoints + the guard
  itself), and `grep -rn HTTP_ORIGIN api/ | grep -v _guard.php` returns 0 (no endpoint
  validates `Origin` on its own) — so the ordering inversion disabled CSRF defence repo-wide.
  Demonstrated on a write route: `POST /api/builds/index.php?action=create` with
  `X-Requested-With` + `Origin: http://evil.example` reached the create handler
  (`400 Invalid test plan id`, i.e. neither 403 nor 401) instead of being rejected.
- Fix: validate `Origin`/`Referer` **first**; `X-Requested-With` now only survives as the
  fallback for the same-origin fetch case where the browser sent neither header, and a
  present-but-unmatched authority header rejects instead of falling through. `Origin` is set
  by the browser and cannot be forged by page JS, `X-Requested-With` can — the strong signal
  is now the primary one. Defense-in-depth: no BFF endpoint emits CORS headers, so a browser
  cannot set XRW cross-origin without a failing preflight.
- Verified with a real browser write: Chrome sends `origin: http://localhost:8082` beside
  `host: localhost:8082`, so `POST /api/builds/index.php` still returns `200` and persists
  the build. Test suite: 20 executable cases (`tmp/suite_1679.py`), 20/20 PASS, and 9/20
  against the pre-fix guard (proving it detects the bug); Event Viewer clean (0
  `ERROR`/`WARNING`).
- Docs: `docs/Bugfix-Issue-1679-bffSameOriginGuard-Origin-Before-XRW.md` + wiki page
  *Bugfix-Issue-1679-bffSameOriginGuard-Origin-Before-XRW*.

### Key bugfix — Custom Field Editor BFF hardening: apply code-review findings M1/M2/m1/m2/m3/m4 (Fixes #1873)
- **auth «oracle» closed** (`api/cfieldsedit/index.php`): the `cfield_management` right on the
  ADDRESSED test project is now asserted BEFORE `cfeResolveProject()` resolves it
  (`cfpaRequireManage()` convention, `api/cfieldstproject/index.php:160-165`). A holder of only
  the GLOBAL right can no longer distinguish a foreign/unreachable project (403
  `no_right_on_project`) from a non-existent one via the init/create-assign routes, and the
  resolve never leaks `tproject_name` on denial; admin keeps the honest 404 for a missing id.
- **verbs whitelisted**: `api/cfieldsedit/index.php` only answers GET/POST; `PUT`/`DELETE`
  now return 405 instead of being accepted.
- **array-payload hardening** (`cfeScalar()`/`cfeInt()`): every request-derived `(string)`/`intval`
  cast is guarded, so a crafted `{"name":["x"],...}` body raises no PHP 8 `Array to string`
  E_WARNING (which `watchPHPErrors()` would persist into `events`) and an array `"id"` never
  `intval()`'s to `1` (wrong-target update/delete).
- **dead show-on combos removed** (`cfieldsEdit.html`): the screen only renders the "Display on
  Test Execution" combo — the design/testplan_design "Display on" combos were a silent no-op
  (legacy `cfieldsEdit.tpl:175-179` had only the execution combo; show_on is derived from
  enable_on server-side).
- `errText()` maps the `{max}` interpolation to the per-field limit (`name`/`label`/`possible_values`)
  instead of always using `name_maxlen`.
- Test suite `Modernize — Issue #1812` rows 35-39 in `tmp/TLU_Test_Cases.md`: **39/39 PASS**,
  Event Viewer clean.

