### UI modernization — Import Platforms (Refs #1632)
- The last fully legacy standalone screen of the Platforms area, `lib/platforms/platformsImport.php`
  (+ `gui/templates/dashio/platforms/platformsImport.tpl`), is modernized as
  `gui/templates/platforms/platformsImport.html` backed by the BFF `api/platformsimport/index.php`
  (`GET ?action=init`, `POST ?action=import`). The Import button of the modern Platforms Management
  screen used to open an inline modal wired to `POST /import` on `api/platforms/index.php`, which
  answers counts only, so the per-platform reporting contract was lost.
- Legacy parity restored: create-or-update-by-name, one `IMPORTED`/`UPDATED` line per platform and
  one skipped line per `<platform>` node without a `<name>`, plus the full legacy file walk
  (`foreach($xml as $platform)` — the root's direct children). `lib/platforms/platformsImport.php`
  is kept as a session-guarded 302 shim, and all `pimp.*` keys exist in the 10 locale bundles.
- Hardening over legacy: the temp copy is unlinked in a `finally` block, `LIBXML_NONET` is explicit,
  libxml errors are returned with line/column so the screen can say *why* a file was rejected, the
  upload cap is enforced server-side (413) and every PHP upload error maps to its own `error_code`.
- The rights gate is split: init needs `platform_view` (or `platform_management`) and import needs
  `platform_management`, so a plain viewer keeps a read-only screen instead of the dead page legacy
  showed, while a user with neither right still gets 403 and no project name or platform count. Every
  403 writes the `audit_security_user_right_missing` event that `checkUserRightsFor()` produced, which
  the JSON BFF had otherwise dropped.
- Four bugs found while testing and fixed: the Upload button stayed disabled for right-holders
  (`busy(false)` ran before the grant was known), the format-documentation link 404'd (partial path
  needed `$basehref`), a platform name repeated in one file called `update(0, …)` and silently lost
  the second node's values, and 405 leaked an untranslated server string.
- Hardened further after the mandatory code review, with 9 new regression cases (Suite 1632 is now
  83/83): a wrong file can no longer be imported — the `<platforms>` root and `<platform>` children
  are required, so a test-case export no longer creates one platform per test case; a failed
  `update()` is reported `IMPORT_FAILED` instead of `UPDATED`; a file without `<is_open>` keeps the
  legacy "closed" default instead of silently re-opening closed platforms; a denied page view is
  audited as `VIEW` (the upload gate stays `IMPORT`); a POST body over `post_max_size` answers 413
  `TOO_LARGE`; the `UPLOAD_ERROR` code is translated client-side and the raw server message is
  escaped before it reaches the DOM; the footer is no longer rendered twice.
- Filed #1634 (pre-existing): the class autoloader wraps `include_once` in `catch (Exception)`, but
  PHP 7+ raises `E_WARNING`, so every missing class permanently adds two Error/Warning rows to the
  Event Viewer. Already fixed independently on the branch by #1593 (`stream_resolve_include_path()`
  guard), so #1634 is closed as its duplicate.
### UI modernization — Direct Links frameset gateway (Refs #1677)
- The direct-links entry point `ltx.php` (`?item=exec|xta2m&build_id=…&feature_id=…|tplan_id=…&tcversion_id=…&platform_id=…[&anchor=…]`)
  is modernized as `gui/templates/links/ltxDirectLink.html` (Dashio: resolved-context card with
  project / plan / build / platform / test case external id / suite / version, clickable chips to
  switch build, platform and any version **linked to the plan** without editing the link, primary
  "Open Execution" / secondary "Open Navigator" actions, access-denied / not-found / error state
  cards carrying the legacy `LTX-0x` markers, TLi18n locale switcher) + BFF `api/ltx/index.php`.
- It was the **last root-level legacy frameset** still rendering Smarty (`main.tpl` /
  `frmInner.tpl` / `workframe.tpl`, via the two-step `ltx.php&load=1` inner frame). Both link
  shapes and all 10 failure outcomes are ported — `LTX-01` bad item / missing user, `LTX-02`
  unknown plan, `LTX-03` xta2m not your tasks, `LTX-04` build not set, `LTX-06` test plan not
  set, `LTX-09` unknown build / version / platform / version-not-in-plan, `LTX-10` unknown
  feature — and each answer returns the machine code **and** the `legacy_code` marker, so the
  raw untranslated legacy `echo`/`die()` strings are gone. Links now hand over to the
  already-modern `execSetResults.html`, `execNavigator.html` and `assignedTcOverview.html`
  instead of the still-legacy `lib/execute/*.php` renderers. `ltx.php` is kept as a
  session-guarded 302 shim that forwards the whole query string, preserving the non-public
  `testlinkInitPage($db, true)` contract, so an anonymous deep link still bounces to
  `login.php?note=expired&destination=…` and every bookmark keeps working.
- Security (each was a real hole in 1.9.20): the `&load=1` inner frame no longer bypasses the
  rights check, `item=xta2m` now enforces the "assigned to **me**" self-check for any user id,
  the version is proved to belong to the addressed plan (`404 version_not_in_plan`), unknown
  `feature_id`/`tcversion_id` no longer dereference a null recordset (PHP 8 fatal), the
  `anchor` parameter is whitelisted instead of interpolated into the iframe `src`, and
  non-numeric ids (`build_id=1abc`, truthy in PHP) are rejected.
- Fixes **#1678** — `testplan::get_parenttestsuites()` recursed on a NULL `parent_id`, producing
  `AND NH.id = ` → MariaDB 1064 and a `log_level=1 DATABASE` Event Viewer row on every hit from
  any screen on the `get_testsuites()` reporting path; guarded with `intval()` + a `<= 0`
  short-circuit (the 2.0.1 `nodes_hierarchy` refactor made `parent_id` nullable).
- Fixes **#1679** — see the dedicated *Key bugfix* entry at the top of the 2.0.1 section:
  `bffSameOriginGuard()` short-circuited on `X-Requested-With` before reading
  `Origin`/`Referer`, so a foreign `Origin` was accepted as same-origin across all guarded
  BFF endpoints. Found from this screen and fixed repo-wide (Origin/Referer validated first,
  XRW demoted to fallback); recorded here as a cross-reference.
- Mandatory code review (subagent): 1 MAJOR + 14 MINOR + 14 NIT, **no security hole**, all
  actionable findings fixed. MAJOR: the platform selector was a silent no-op — `Apply`
  re-emitted a `feature_id` whose `testplan_tcversions` row then overwrote the chosen
  `platform_id`; an explicit platform now always wins and the feature platform is only a
  default. MINORs: the "No platform" option could never take effect (BFF *and* screen used
  truthiness instead of parameter presence, in `applySettings()` and in the `currentParams()`
  request builder); an ambiguous multi-platform `testplan_tcversions` row made the reported
  feature id non-deterministic; the DB was connected **before** the auth gate, so a down
  database answered HTTP 200 with a raw `dbms_msg`; `item=xta2m` forwarded `build_id`
  unvalidated; one extra `SELECT` per linked version (N+1) plus duplicate `<option>` values
  for a multi-platform version; the header comment claimed `LTX-05`/`LTX-08` branches that
  never existed and the docs said "7 machine codes" where 19 are emitted; 2 unreachable
  i18n keys removed.
- Test suite: 96 executable cases (`tmp/suite_1677.py`), 96/96 PASS, including 18 regression
  cases pinning the review fixes; Event Viewer clean (0 `ERROR`/`WARNING`, 0 `DATABASE`).

