  here): `lib/reqmgrsystems/reqMgrSystemEdit.php` returns HTTP 500 when `doAction` is
  missing or unknown, because `reqMgrSystemEdit.php:126` throws an uncaught `Exception` and
  the whitelist in `reqMgrSystemCommands.class.php:38-39` has no key for the empty value.
- Sibling defect found by code review of #1592 and filed as **#1625** (not fixed here):
  `reqMgrSystemView.php?id=<n>` returns HTTP 500 with an empty body for **any** id, because
  `checkConnection()` reaches `tlReqMgrSystem.class.php:616-621`, which instantiates
  `contoursoapInterface` — a class absent from the repository. Pre-existing (`git cat-file -e`
  fails at the baseline commit too) and unreachable from the #1592 change, which only
  assigns a variable nothing reads. Same missing file as #1593 but a fatal rather than a
  warning, hence tracked separately.

### Key bugfix — Req. Management System "Check connection" empty HTTP 500 (Fixes #1625)
- Key bugfix #1625: the legacy Dashio Req. Management System list answered
  **HTTP 500 with a 0-byte body** for *any* `?id=` — existing row or not — and logged 4
  `E_WARNING` rows per request (5 for a non-existent `id`).
  `reqMgrSystemView.php:36` calls `tlReqMgrSystem::checkConnection()` (`:616-622`),
  which built a class name with
  `getImplementationForType()` (`:111-115`) and instantiated it with **no existence
  check**: `type=1` resolves to `contoursoapInterface`, whose file is not shipped and
  never was (`git log --all -- '*contour*'` is empty — only the abstract
  `reqMgrSystemInterface` base exists in `lib/reqmgrsystemintegration/`), and a
  non-existent id reaches `new NULL` because `getByID()` returns `NULL`. Both raise an
  uncaught `Error` — not an `Exception`, so the `catch (Exception)` of the sibling
  `getInterfaceObject()` never applied — which PHP 8 aborts before a byte is flushed.
  Pre-existing since 1.9.6; the *empty* body is a PHP 8 + `display_errors=Off` symptom

  (the `Error` fires while the page is still being built, and nothing has been flushed
  yet).

  Fix: `checkConnection()` returns `false` when the row is missing
  or the implementation class cannot be loaded (the caller maps it to `'ko'` and
  `reqMgrSystemView.tpl:52-53` already draws the existing localized
  `reqmgrsystem_check_ko` badge — **no new i18n key**), the controller stamps
  `connection_status` only on a row that exists (otherwise `?id=999` traded a 500 for a
  phantom empty grid row, the #1618 family), and `getAll()`'s `checkEnv` block gets the
  same `is_null($impl) || !@class_exists($impl) || !is_callable([$impl,'checkEnv'])`
  guard already landed for the twins `tlIssueTracker` (#1617) and `tlCodeTracker`
  (#1597) — which also removes the two `include_once` events per row per load that #1593
  tracks for this screen.
  Code review then found the SAME defect duplicated in
  `reqMgrSystemCommands::checkConnection()` (the edit screen's whitelisted
  `doAction=checkConnection` route, measured `500`/0 B pre-fix); the duplicate is deleted
  and the method now delegates to the single hardened `tlReqMgrSystem::checkConnection()`,
  keeping its `'ok' : 'ko'` mapping. Verified: `?id=<row>` 500/0 B/4 events -> 200/10994 B/
  KO badge/0 events; `?id=999` 500 -> 200 with no phantom row; no-`id` loads 2 events -> 0;
  `doAction=checkConnection` 500 -> 200; the two twins and the modernized
  `api/reqmgrsystems` BFF unchanged; browser console clean. Regression suite 1625 31/31
  PASS (`bash tmp/verify_1625.sh`, exit 0; pre-fix baseline 11 FAIL / exit 1, so the
  harness is discriminating). Sibling defects found while testing/reviewing and filed,
  not fixed: **#1626** (a row whose `type` is not a key of `$systems` still logs 6
  `E_WARNING` per load), **#1627** (`reqMgrSystemEdit.php` without a whitelisted
  `doAction` is a hard 500), **#1628** (`Undefined array key "checkConnection"` on the
  route this fix unblocked) and **#1629** (the third unguarded `new` in
  `getInterfaceObject()`, an unverified code-path reading). (Fixes #1625)

### Key bugfix — Req. Management System list: no E_WARNING for an unknown type code (Fixes #1626)
- Key bugfix #1626 (the noise half of the #1625 family, filed as a sibling by the
  #1625 run): one `reqmgrsystems` row whose `type` is **not** a key of
  `tlReqMgrSystem::$systems` made **every** load of the Req. Management System list
  write 5 `E_WARNING` rows into `events` — 5 for the plain list, 8 for `?id=<n>`,
  and 5 for the **modern** `GET /api/reqmgrsystems/index.php` as well (both go
  through `getAll()`; the issue only named the legacy URL).

  **Root cause.** `tlReqMgrSystem::$types` is *projected* from `$systems` in
  `getTypes()` (`lib/functions/tlReqMgrSystem.class.php:99`), so an unknown
  `type` has no `types` entry either — `types` is a strict subset of `systems`'s
  keys, and there is exactly one writer and four readers in the file. Three of
  those readers had no `isset()`:

  | Site | Diagnostics per bad row |
  |---|---|
  | `getAll()` `$this->types[$item['type']]` ×2 (`:522-523`) | 2× `Undefined array key <type>` |
  | `getImplementationForType()` `$this->systems[$system]` (`:113`) | 1× `Undefined array key <type>` |
  | `getImplementationForType()` `$spec['type']` / `$spec['api']` (`:114`) | 2× `Trying to access array offset on null` |
  | `getLinkedTo()` `$ret['verboseType']` (`:595`) | 1× `Undefined array key <type>` |

  **Why it did not fatal, and why that is not a defence.** #1625 had already
  wrapped `getAll()`'s env probe in
  `is_null($impl) || !@class_exists($impl) || !is_callable([$impl, 'checkEnv'])`,
  so the garbage class name was discarded and the page kept answering 200 with
  the row rendered. That guard stops the *fatal*; the two `$this->types` reads and
  the two reads inside `getImplementationForType()` happen before/outside it.
  Separately, `getImplementationForType()` returned the literal string
  `"Interface"` (`null . null . 'Interface'`) — a *valid-looking* class name that
  any caller may then instantiate.

  **Fix** (the shape #1597 / #1617 already proved on the two twins — this is a
  missing port, not a new regression):
  * `getImplementationForType()` returns `null` for a type that is not a key of
    `$systems`, so the garbage class name can never be composed
    (verbatim `tlCodeTracker.class.php:114-137` / `tlIssueTracker.class.php:168-190`).
  * `getAll()` and `getLinkedTo()` read `$this->types[...]` through a guarded
    `$typeDescr` local (verbatim `tlCodeTracker.class.php:570-571` /
    `tlIssueTracker.class.php:622-623`), so an unknown type degrades to an empty
    description and the row stays **visible and repairable** — which is the
    issue's own "Expected" and both twins' behaviour.
  * `api/reqmgrsystems/index.php:105` gains `!is_null($impl) &&` before
    `@class_exists($impl)`: `class_exists(NULL)` is an `E_DEPRECATED` on PHP 8.1+
    and `method_exists(NULL, …)` is a **TypeError**; the `&&` short-circuit is
    what makes the list route safe by construction rather than by luck. The branch
    was also **inverted** to the shape `getAll():562-566` and
    `api/codetracker/index.php` use — an implementation that cannot be probed now
    sets `env_check_ok = false`. It did not before, so the legacy grid (which
    requests `checkEnv=true` and painted a red badge) and the modern payload
    (`"env_check_ok": true`) disagreed about exactly the row this issue is about;
    they now agree. That is the ONE field of the BFF list payload this fix changes.
  * `api/reqmgrsystems/index.php:302-306` (`POST /<id>/check_connection`) answers a
    NULL implementation with `Interface for type <n> not implemented` instead of
    echoing the garbage class name back (`Interface Interface not implemented`).
    Plain English, like every other message this BFF file returns — so this fix
    deliberately does NOT localize it, and no locale bundle was touched.

  **Rejected alternatives.** `@` / `error_reporting()` — hides every future
  diagnostic in the same code, including real bugs, and diverges from the two
  classes that already solved this. Dropping the unusable row from the listing —
  the manager then cannot *see* the bad `type` to repair it. Guarding only the
  three call sites in the legacy view — the modern BFF list, `getLinkedTo()` and
  the `?id=` route would keep logging.

  **Caller audit (all 5 `getImplementationForType()` call sites).** 3 needed no
  change: `getByID()` (`:321`) is already NULL-tolerant on the
  `checkConnection()` path because `:655` guards with
  `!isset($xx['implementation'])` and `isset(NULL)` is `false`; `getAll()`
  (`:530`) already has #1625's `is_null($impl)`;
  `lib/ajax/getreqmgrsystemcfgtemplate.php:29` and
  `api/reqmgrsystems/index.php:159` are both preceded by an
  `isset($types[$type])` gate, and since `types` is projected from `systems` the
  key is guaranteed present. **The second consumer of
  `getByID()['implementation']` is `getInterfaceObject()` (`:642-643`), which is
  deliberately NOT fixed here** — its unguarded `new $iname` is a standing defect
  tracked as **#1629**, and it behaves identically before this change
  (`new "Interface"` and `new NULL` both raise an uncatchable `Error`, so the
  outcome is the same empty 500). `api/reqspec/index.php:1331` was adjusted in the
  same pass: `getLinkedTo()` now always sets `verboseType` (it is `''` for an
  unknown type), which made that expression's
  `isset($linked['verboseType']) ? … : $linked['type']` fallback permanently dead,
  so the test is now on the VALUE (`!== ''`).

  **Verified on a freshly imported DB.** 9 requests — legacy list, `?id=` on a
  bad-type *and* a good-type row, BFF list, `meta/types`,
  `meta/cfg_template?type=1` and `?type=99`, both legacy ajax cfg-template calls
  — **0 new `events` rows** (5 per request pre-fix). A/B harness loading
  `origin/sebiboga`'s copy of the class and the fixed one in two PHP processes
  against the same database: **10 diagnostics pre-fix vs 0 post-fix**, with every
  non-warning value byte-identical (`impl(1)='contoursoapInterface'`,
  `typeDescr='contour (Interface: soap)'`, `getLinkedTo().verboseType=''`); the
  BFF list JSON is byte-identical to the pre-fix capture. In-browser A/B by
  swapping only the class file back to `origin/sebiboga` reproduces 5 events;
  `git checkout --` restores the fix and the next load adds 0. `php -l` clean on
  both files. **No new i18n key and no locale bundle touched, no template change**
  (the bad row keeps its empty Type cell, matching the issue-tracker twin; the
  code-tracker twin additionally shows a `ct.msg.invalidType` badge via a
  `typeKnown` field that the reqmgr BFF still lacks). Regression suite 1626 22/22 PASS (`bash tmp/verify_1626.sh`, exit 0; pre-fix baseline 16 PASS / 6 FAIL / exit 1 with only the class file reverted, so the harness is discriminating).

  **Three defects found while testing / reviewing were filed, NOT fixed here**
  (each is a different file or a different defect, and each needs its own
  regression matrix):
  * **#1714** — `requirement_spec_mgr::get_by_id()` interpolates an EMPTY
    `RSPEC_REV.id = ` into a WHERE clause when `get_last_active_version()` returns
    false (1064 syntax error + `E_WARNING` at
    `requirement_spec_mgr.class.php:186`); same family as #1708.
  * **#1715** — `tlCodeTracker::getLinkedTo()` (`:643-648`) still carries the SAME
    two unguarded `$this->types[…]` / `$this->systems[…][…]` reads this fix just
    removed from the reqmgr twin (3 warnings per call, reachable from every
    project read). #1597 hardened the other two methods of that class and missed
    this one; `tlIssueTracker::getLinkedTo():717` and (as of this fix)
    `tlReqMgrSystem::getLinkedTo():621` both have the guard — `tlCodeTracker` is
    now the last of the three without it.
  * **#1716** — both `lang_get()` keys used by
    `lib/ajax/getreqmgrsystemcfgtemplate.php:41,46`
    (`reqmgrsystem_interface_not_implemented`, `reqmgrsystem_invalid_type`) exist
    in **no** locale file, so the endpoint answers the literal
    `LOCALIZE: <key>` marker to the browser and logs an Event Viewer row. (Fixes #1626)


### KEY BUGFIX — `reqMgrSystemCommands::initGuiBean()` read an undefined label for 2 of its 7 whitelisted actions (Fixes #1628)
- `lib/reqmgrsystems/reqMgrSystemCommands.class.php` dispatched 7 action names via
  `guiOpWhiteList`, but the `$obj->l18n` table it built covered only 5. The unconditional
  `ucfirst($obj->l18n[$caller])` therefore raised a PHP 8 `E_WARNING "Undefined array key"`
  (plus a `ucfirst(): Passing null to parameter #1` `E_DEPRECATED`) for **both** `checkConnection`
  and `delete` — every call, surfaced as an Event Viewer row by `watchPHPErrors`. The report named
  only `checkConnection`; `delete` is the identical defect on the identical line.
- Both actions are now registered in the `init_labels()` call onto label codes that already ship in
  the legacy locale bundles (`btn_check_connection`, `btn_delete`), and the read is wrapped in an
  `isset()` guard so the whitelist and the label table can drift again without emitting warnings.
- **Trade-off, measured:** `btn_check_connection` ships in 7 of 19 bundles and `btn_delete` in 18,
  so in the remaining locales `lang_get()` back-fills from `en_GB` and records one `L18N` (level
  32) audit row per key — the same, already-pre-existing behaviour the function has for its other
  five labels. Net: 0 Warning/Error rows everywhere, 2 extra level-32 audit rows in 13 locales.
  Translating 13 bundles is out of scope for a one-line label fix.


### Key bugfix — autoloader no longer logs 2 E_WARNINGs for a class this fork does not ship (Refs #1593)
- Key bugfix #1593: the application's **only** class loader, `tlAutoload()`
  (`lib/functions/common.php:52` registers it), did an **unconditional**
  `include_once $classFileName . '.class.php'`. `include_once` on an absent file is not an
  exception — it raises **two** `E_WARNING`s (`Failed to open stream` + `Failed opening ... for
  inclusion`) and returns `false`, so the BitNami `try { } catch (Exception) { }` underneath it
  could never catch them and `watchPHPErrors()` (`lib/functions/logger.class.php:1407`) wrote
  **both** into the `events` table on every request that touched a class missing from this fork.
  Because `register_shutdown_function("shutdownLogger")` commits the open logger transaction
  even on a fatal, the two rows survived the HTTP 500 as well, so the Event Viewer was polluted
  by exactly the requests that were already broken for a different reason.
  Live instance: `contoursoapInterface`, the `implementation` of `reqmgrsystems.type=1`
  (`tlReqMgrSystem.class.php:33`), a class that is absent and never was (`find . -iname
  '*contour*'` → nothing, `git log --all -- '*contour*'` empty).
  **The report's own repro no longer warned** — #1625 had already silenced the two
  `checkConnection()` call sites with `@class_exists()` — but the loader defect was untouched
  and still reachable through the *unguarded* instantiation in
  `tlReqMgrSystem::getInterfaceObject()` (`:617`): `reqSpecSearch.php:34` →
  `reqSpecCommands::__construct()` → `reqSpecCommands.class.php:44` → `new $iname` →
  autoloader. Measured pre-fix: `GET /lib/requirements/reqSpecSearch.php` → 500 with **2** new
  `E_WARNING` rows naming `contoursoapInterface.class.php` and `common.php` line 122
  (attribution control: `reqMgrSystemView.php` on the same session adds 0).
  Fix: **resolve the file, then include it** — `stream_resolve_include_path()` first (the same
  `include_path` order `include()` itself uses), falling back to `is_file()` for the current
  working directory, and `return` quietly when the target is not a real file, so the class
  simply stays undefined and PHP raises its usual `Error: Class not found` at the actual
  `new`/`class_exists()` site where the callers already decide how to degrade. No caller was
  touched, no i18n bundle was touched, and a code review over 120 class names (108 shipped +
  absent/edge names) measured **0** resolution changes and 0 new diagnostics.
  Also corrected the now-stale `common.php:122` cross-reference left in
  `tlReqMgrSystem.class.php:647` by #1625.
  Verified: primary repro 2 events → **0**; the report's own repro stays 200/0 events; the
  loader still autoloads flat classes and classes from sub-directory `include_path` entries
  (`lib/issuetrackerintegration/`, `lib/codetrackerintegration/`,
  `lib/reqmgrsystemintegration/`); a 9-screen app-wide sweep and a browser pass (Dashboard,
  Requirements Design → Search Requirements) add **0** `E_WARNING`/Error rows and **0** console
  errors. Regression suite #1593 26 PASS / 0 FAIL (`bash tmp/verify_1593.sh`, exit 0; pre-fix
  baseline 4 FAIL / exit 1, so the harness is discriminating).
  **Deliberately NOT fixed here** (separate issue): the HTTP 500 of the same request, i.e. the
  unguarded `new` in `getInterfaceObject()` whose `catch (Exception)` cannot catch a PHP 8
  `Error` — **#1629**; this fix only removes the warning noise and must not mask that fatal.
  Also found while testing and filed separately, not fixed: `third_party/phpxmlrpc/lib/xmlrpc.inc`
  uses `$temp =& new xmlrpcval(...)`, a `ParseError` on PHP 8, so autoloading
  `tracxmlrpcInterface` fatals identically before and after this change (**#1635**).
  (Refs #1593)

### Key bugfix — TLi18n locale selection persistence (Refs #1586)
- Key bugfix #1586: an explicit language switch in the locale switcher now
  survives navigation, so every modernized screen that returns to a launcher
  (Cancel/Back, no `?locale=` in the URL) keeps the chosen language again.
- `gui/templates/i18n/i18n.js`: `detectLocale()` reads `localStorage('tl_locale')`
  again — resolution order `?locale=` ▸ manual switch ▸ DB profile ▸ `en`, as the
  module header always documented; the profile lookup still never writes the
