### UI modernization — Requirements Bulk Assignment (Refs #1595)
- New modern screen `gui/templates/requirements/reqTcBulkAssign.html` for the legacy
  Requirements Bulk Assignment grid (`lib/requirements/reqTcAssign.php` in
  testsuite/bulk mode + `gui/templates/dashio/requirements/reqTcBulkAssignment.tpl`),
  which was reachable only from the Test Specification tree
  (`listTestCases.php?feature=assignReqs`). It is *not* a duplicate of the
  `assignReqs.html` "Test Suite (Bulk)" picker: the new screen is a coverage grid —
  every requirement of the chosen spec with a `n/m test cases of this suite already
  linked` chip, plus bulk Assign **and** Unassign (legacy offered only Assign).
  Dashio popup with the legacy `bulk_req_assign_msg` / `bulk_req_assign_no_test_cases`
  warnings, context card (test project / test suite / deep test-case count /
  requirement-spec selector), check-uncheck-all, scope column, confirm dialog,
  feedback box, empty states and localized 401/403/404 cards; 36 `rtcb.*` keys in
  the 10 locale bundles.
- New BFF `api/reqtcbassign/index.php`: `GET ?action=init` (context, deep
  `get_testcases_deep()` count, per-requirement `linked_count`, spec options),
  `POST ?action=bulkassign` (`requirement_mgr::bulkAssignLatestREQVTCV()`, legacy
  1:1 and idempotent) and `POST ?action=unassign` (removes exactly the open
  coverage rows the grid created). Session auth, `req_tcase_link_management`,
  `bffSameOriginGuard`, 400/401/403/404/405 JSON contract, and one aggregated
  audit event per effective operation.
- Hardening beyond legacy: the test suite is proven to belong to the test project,
  the requirement-spec id (request *and* the persisted session memory) is proven
  to belong to that project, `tsuite_id` must be a real test-suite node, the
  project must have requirements enabled, and the submitted requirement ids are
  intersected with the requirements that really live on the submitted spec — so a
  forged `req_id`/`idSRS` from another spec/project can no longer be read or
  linked through this route (the hole tracked by #1085 for the legacy
  controller).
- Entry points: `$actions->reqTcBulkAssign` in `lib/functions/common.php` and a
  new "Requirements Bulk Assignment" button in the Test Specification suite view;
  `lib/requirements/reqTcAssign.php` is now a session-guarded 302 shim
  (anonymous -> login, `?id=` forwarded as `tsuite_id`).
- Key bugfix #1596: `gui/templates/testcases/testSpec.html` gated both
  requirement-linking buttons on `ctx.reqEnabled`, which `init()` never sets, so
  the pre-existing per-test-case "Assign Requirements" button and the new
  suite-level one were silently never rendered; both now use
  `ctx.options.requirementsEnabled`, the flag the context API actually returns.
- Key bugfix: the repo vendors Bootstrap 3.4.1, so the confirm dialog loaded a
  non-existent `bootstrap.bundle.min.js` and threw on `bootstrap.Modal`; the
  screen now uses the jQuery `modal('show'/'hide')` API plus the `data-target`
  attribute BS3 requires to dismiss a modal (header "x" and Cancel).
- Key bugfix: the audit events passed the requirements table as `$objectID`, so
  the Event Viewer showed no object; they are now bound to the test suite and no
  longer written for a no-op. Event Viewer hygiene: 0 ERROR/WARNING rows.
- Security fixes from the mandatory code review:
  - stored XSS: the test-suite name reached the warning bar and the confirm
    dialog as raw HTML; it is now escaped, and all placeholder interpolation uses
    a replacer callback so a name containing `$&`/`` $` ``/`$'` can never rewrite
    the sentence;
  - IDOR: `idSRS` was only checked for `> 0`, so a spec of another project could
    be read or used to create/delete cross-project links — the spec is now
    resolved against the current test project (404 init / 400 writes);
  - the right is now evaluated with `hasRight(..., getAccess = true)`, matching
    legacy `pageAccessCheck()`: a user holding the right only through a *global*
    role can no longer touch a **private** test project they are not a member of;
  - a refused access is audited (`SECURITY` / `testprojects`) like legacy did,
    "nothing selected" is a 400 (the screen renders the message), the action
    buttons stay disabled on a suite without test cases (legacy rendered no
    button), `linked_count` counts only the open links `unassign` can remove, a
    test-case node id is rejected with 404, the footer uses the translated
    `footers.reqTcBulkAssign` key, every row regains the legacy requirement
    version editor link, the checkboxes get accessible titles, and responses are
    sent as `application/json; charset=utf-8` + `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`.
  Regression suite 1595: 63/63 PASS.

### UI modernization — Remote Test Automation Execution (Refs #1587)
- New BFF `api/tcautoexec/index.php` (GET `?action=init` = context + runnable
  node list with the automation server resolved per node, POST `?action=run` =
  per-test-case XML-RPC results) for the last standalone `lib/testcases/*`
