### KEY BUGFIX — Requirement Coverage Tree BFF: `fetch_array()` answers `false`, so a count query logged an Event Viewer warning (Fixes #1766 follow-up)
- `activeCoverageCount()` dereferenced the result of `$db->fetch_array()` with an `is_null()` check;
  an exhausted rowset answers **false**, which produced `Trying to access array offset on false`
  (`log_level=2`). The coverage row read also used `$row['tc_external_id']` / `['name']` /
  `['version']` without a guard, producing `Undefined array key "external_id"`. Both are now
  `empty()` / `isset()` guarded; exercising every action leaves the `events` table empty. (Refs #1765)

### KEY BUGFIX — Trac XML-RPC transport: the phpxmlrpc wire layer fataled on PHP 8, killing every `ticket.get`/`ticket.create` and the bug-link renderer (Fixes #1764)
- `third_party/phpxmlrpc/lib/xmlrpc.inc` used the PHP 4 functions **`each()`** (removed in PHP 8.0)
  and **`split()`** (removed in PHP 7.0) at **15 sites**, so the *first* command the Trac
  interface sends — `tracxmlrpcInterface::sendCmd()` → `xmlrpcmsg::createPayload()` →
  `xmlrpcval::serialize()` (`xmlrpc.inc:2946`) — died with `Call to undefined function each()`,
  taking `getIssue()`, `checkBugIDExistence()`, `addIssue()` and `buildViewBugLink()` with it.
- Ported as: `foreach` walks for full-array iterations, guarded `key()`/`current()` reads for
  single pairs (`reset()` semantics preserved, including `null` vs `false` on an empty value),
  `preg_split('/\r?\n/')` for header parsing, and `structeach()` re-implemented on
  `key()`/`current()`/`next()` — exactly PHP's own `each()` algorithm, returning the same
  `(0, 'value', 1, 'key')` slots, so the public contract is unchanged.
- Found while verifying the port end to end: `xmlrpcmsg::parseResponse()` passed
  **`count($data)`** (a TypeError on strings since PHP 8.0) as the `xml_parse()` length, so the
  response side fataled too → now `strlen($data)`.
- Verified **byte-identical** behaviour against the pre-port library (with `each()`/`split()`
  reconstructed as a polyfill) over 60+ observables, plus a live TCP round trip: a valid
  `methodCall` goes out, `set-cookie` is captured and the struct response decodes. (Refs #1764)

### Screen — Test Case Summary `tcSummary` (Refs #1767)
- Modernizes the last legacy-only read-only slice: `lib/ajax/gettestcasesummary.php`, the ExtJS
  `tTip()` tooltip backend of the 1.9.20 Add/Remove Test Cases workframe
  (`gui/templates/dashio/plan/planAddTC_m1.tpl:58`, `planAddTCJS.inc.tpl`). New screen
  `gui/templates/testcases/tcSummary.html` (Dashio: teal header + dark toolbar with
  Refresh / Open test case / Close, context card with test project, prefix, `#PREFIX-N` chip,
  version chip, `latest version` chip and suite path, summary card, TLi18n locale switcher).
- **KEY BUGFIX (security)** — the legacy endpoint performed **no authorization check at all**:
  `testlinkInitPage()` only validated the session and `tcase_id` came straight from `$_REQUEST`,
  so any authenticated user could read the summary of a test case of **any** test project (same
  class as #1696 / #1679). It also echoed the stored RichEdit blob **raw** into the caller DOM
  where the tooltip injected it as HTML (stored XSS), and dereferenced the nullable results of
  `testcase::get_last_version_info()` / `get_by_id()` unguarded.
- New BFF `api/tcsummary/index.php` (`GET|HEAD ?action=summary&tcase_id=N[&tcversion_id=V][&tproject_id=P]`):
  session auth + `bffSameOriginGuard`, the **owning** project proven by walking `nodes_hierarchy`
  up from the test case node, `mgt_view_tc` enforced on it, the requested version proven to belong
  to that test case, `tproject_id` treated as a client-side assertion (mismatch → 404), strict
  positive ids and stable 400/401/403/404/405/500 codes. The summary is returned as **data** and
  the screen renders it as escaped plain text (block tags collapsed to newlines, entities decoded
  once), so the XSS sink is gone.
- `lib/ajax/gettestcasesummary.php` is now a session-guarded launcher: a browser navigation 302s to
  the modern popup with `tcase_id` / `tcversion_id` / context preserved, an XHR or crawler gets 405
  pointing at the BFF, an anonymous caller still bounces to
  `login.php?note=expired&destination=...` (legacy `testlinkInitPage()` contract). Wired via
  `$actions->tcSummary` in `lib/functions/common.php`.
- The summary affordance is **restored** in `gui/templates/plans/planAddTCView.html`, which had
  dropped the feature entirely: a per-row button (with an `aria-label`) opens the popup for the
  version selected in that row (or the newest active one). It is also wired into the modern Test
  Case Viewer, `gui/templates/testcases/tcView.html`, as one **Show summary** button per version
  card, so `$actions->tcSummary` has live consumers.
- **Mandatory code review (subagent) found no security hole in the read path** but 4 should-fix
  items, all fixed: the BFF resolved the version **before** the rights check, which let any
  authenticated user tell an existing test case node from a missing one and probe for valid
  version ids (now the version is resolved only after `mgt_view_tc`, and a not-entitled caller with
  no asserted project gets one opaque 404); the icon-only button's accessible name said "Open test
  case" instead of "Show summary" (wrong key + no `aria-label`); `footers.tcSummary` never rendered
  because it was appended **after** `TLi18n.apply()` (now static markup); the shim has **three**
  live ExtJS tooltip callers, not two (`tl-classic/plan/planAddTC_m1.tpl` was missed) and, because
  Ext 3.4 sends `X-Requested-With`, they now get an empty tooltip by design - the Dashio workframe
  gets the summary through its own button instead, and the docblock says so. Also fixed: the shim
  now also honours the inactivity window and detects modern XHR via `Sec-Fetch-Dest`/`Accept`, the
  BFF sends `Cache-Control: no-store`, and the "Stored source" blob is a real collapsed `<details>`.
